WEBVTT

01:22.086 --> 01:26.934
Hello New York! I'm Bobby Rydell.
And I'm glad to be here.

01:29.372 --> 01:34.354
Thank you all for coming to see us tonight.
It's Saturday night in the Copa!

01:34.482 --> 01:36.700
We think that we're gonna
have a great time tonight.

01:36.724 --> 01:38.847
We're gonna do our best
to make sure of that.

01:38.929 --> 01:43.175
As always a very special thanks to
Mr. Jules Podell for having us out.

01:43.538 --> 01:45.434
Let's get started.

02:16.301 --> 02:17.886
Hello sweetheart.

02:17.910 --> 02:19.488
Here is my coat.

02:19.512 --> 02:21.327
And you see this here hat?

02:21.351 --> 02:23.614
I want you to guard it with your life.

02:23.843 --> 02:27.364
- It was a gift from my mother.
- Yes, Mr. Loscudo.

02:27.969 --> 02:29.458
Yeah. That's for you.

02:29.883 --> 02:31.270
Thank you sir.

02:31.734 --> 02:32.723
Joey!

02:32.758 --> 02:35.583
- Hey Carmine! How are you pal?
- Good to see you.

02:36.422 --> 02:38.215
Oh thank you! That's unnecessary.

02:38.443 --> 02:40.018
Come on! Let's go. On the album.

02:40.259 --> 02:42.683
I saw this kid Bobby Rydell
two and a half years

02:42.707 --> 02:45.096
ago in South Philly.
Nobody knew who he was.

02:45.120 --> 02:46.344
They know now.

02:47.120 --> 02:48.214
Hey!

02:48.238 --> 02:49.609
Gimme Loscudo's hat.

02:49.626 --> 02:53.774
- But he said to guard it...
- I know, I heard. Give it to me. A'right?

03:10.464 --> 03:11.821
Tony Lip!

03:35.018 --> 03:36.626
You put your hands
on me, you punk?

03:36.650 --> 03:39.107
Do yourself a favor. Go
home with your friends.

03:39.131 --> 03:43.042
You don't tell me where to go! Do you
know who I am?! I'm goin' back in there!

04:10.295 --> 04:15.006
You tell Jules Lipobdell. If I don't get
my hat I'm gonna burn this joint down.

04:15.030 --> 04:16.495
I swear to God it's
gonna turn up.

04:16.519 --> 04:21.422
Really? You tell that fat Jew bastard I
don't get my hat I'll burn Copa down!

04:26.445 --> 04:29.153
I'm gonna have to go back
to driving garbage trucks.

04:29.976 --> 04:31.856
Jesus Christ!

04:32.388 --> 04:34.339
Screw those! He's out of his mind.

04:36.588 --> 04:38.225
We earned our money tonight.

04:38.572 --> 04:40.102
Lip, I thought you
were gonna kill that guy.

04:40.126 --> 04:40.835
Yeah!

04:41.150 --> 04:42.350
Better him than me.

04:44.499 --> 04:46.539
So... What are you gonna do
while we're closed?

04:46.894 --> 04:49.906
I don't know. Maybe go work
at my Uncle's pizza joint.

04:51.574 --> 04:54.716
- You?
- I'm gonna drink for 2 months.

05:00.647 --> 05:01.894
Take me home, Lip.

05:03.897 --> 05:04.943
See you Carmine.

05:04.967 --> 05:07.878
- No! You shouldn't. That shouldn't happen.
- I don't wanna be a...

05:09.795 --> 05:10.995
My hat!

05:12.190 --> 05:15.328
Heard it was missing,
so I looked into it.

05:16.003 --> 05:19.343
- I wanted to kill that broad.
- No. No. Wasn't her fault.

05:19.464 --> 05:21.929
Who had the balls to clip Joey's hat?

05:22.251 --> 05:25.811
- Don't worry about it, I took care of him.
- Yeah! I hope you gave him some beating.

05:26.908 --> 05:29.944
Here. Take this. Put
it in your kick.

05:30.323 --> 05:33.530
No. No thanks. It was a
pleasure, Mr. Loscudo.

05:33.831 --> 05:35.640
Bullshit! Take it.

05:36.236 --> 05:40.247
And from now on, you don't call
me Mr Loscude, ya hear me?

05:40.271 --> 05:42.338
I'm your pal Joey.

07:06.249 --> 07:07.590
Good morning.

07:08.296 --> 07:09.496
Good night!

07:18.056 --> 07:22.688
- Come on, Roger! Hit one out!
- Johnny quite! You're gonna jinx it.

07:22.712 --> 07:25.540
Hey Johnny, think you can
yell a little louder?

07:25.564 --> 07:27.905
- Maris is up.
- Yeah, so am I now.

07:29.054 --> 07:30.734
What the hell are you
guys doing here?

07:31.612 --> 07:34.117
We came over to give Dolores company.

07:37.104 --> 07:38.664
Come on!

07:58.857 --> 08:01.260
Come on Roger! Please!

08:02.068 --> 08:03.909
- I'll walk you out.
- Sure.

08:04.662 --> 08:07.575
When did you get back to
these board games? Come on!

08:07.599 --> 08:09.174
Thank you so much!

08:19.223 --> 08:22.977
We got it!
We got it! Yeah!

08:31.782 --> 08:34.911
Do it again. Let's do it again.
Come on baby!

08:34.957 --> 08:38.063
No! Tony, go get dressed.
We're gonna eat.

08:39.889 --> 08:41.076
Alright!

08:41.100 --> 08:43.386
No game seven. No game seven.

08:54.207 --> 08:58.852
From thy bounty through
Christ our Lord, Amen.

09:00.068 --> 09:03.091
And if anyone hears of a job for
Tony, let us know.

09:03.115 --> 09:05.909
- Dolor! Please.
- What?

09:06.310 --> 09:08.755
- What happened? Did you get fired?
- No.

09:08.779 --> 09:13.112
No, The Copa's closing for repairs. So he
just needs something for a couple months.

09:21.594 --> 09:24.497
All the people he knows, he'll find
something in no time.

09:24.563 --> 09:27.568
Oh. He had a great job at the
sanitation department.

09:27.860 --> 09:29.755
You shouldn't have
punched out the foreman.

09:30.287 --> 09:31.932
He shouldn't have woke me up.

09:33.412 --> 09:34.948
That's Tony.

09:55.546 --> 09:57.695
I'm tellin' you, this is
gonna be the easiest fifty

09:57.719 --> 09:59.817
- bucks you ever gonna made.
- Yeah we'll see.

10:00.351 --> 10:02.575
Hey! There they are.

10:02.624 --> 10:03.824
Hi Johnny.

10:03.828 --> 10:05.555
- Tony!
- Hey Paulie. How you doing?

10:05.579 --> 10:08.142
I'm good. I'm good. So,
Johnny here tells me you ate

10:08.166 --> 10:11.293
forty-eight White Castle
burgers all in one sitting.

10:11.578 --> 10:13.208
Cheese burgers.

10:13.305 --> 10:15.848
- You tell them Frankie.
- I don't believe you.

10:16.086 --> 10:18.059
What do I care if you believe me?

10:18.594 --> 10:19.577
Hey Gorman.

10:19.601 --> 10:23.568
- What's the record here for Hotdogs?
- Eighteen. Fat Paulie.

10:23.592 --> 10:27.324
- Why wasn't Lip in on that contest?
- What contest? I was hungry.

10:28.896 --> 10:30.932
Bet's simple. Half a C-note.

10:31.037 --> 10:34.237
- Most hotdogs in an hour wins.
- With toppings.

10:35.829 --> 10:37.029
What the hell you weigh?

10:37.153 --> 10:40.434
- Two sixty.
- Aaaaay. Your left ass weighs two sixty.

10:40.458 --> 10:43.017
May my mother-in-law drop dead
on the spot if I'm lyin'.

10:46.202 --> 10:48.370
- Alright. You're up.
- Good.

10:50.318 --> 10:54.354
Pick it up Lip! The baby
elephant just hit nineteen!

10:54.693 --> 10:57.081
Let's go Lip! Let's go. Come on.

10:58.573 --> 11:05.539
You are embarrassing. You're embarrassing
your son. He's killing you.

11:12.478 --> 11:14.670
- Hey Nicky. You do your homework?
- Yep.

11:14.752 --> 11:15.952
Good.

11:17.714 --> 11:20.652
- Where have you been?
- Gorman's.

11:20.676 --> 11:22.860
I'm making dinner!

11:24.967 --> 11:28.246
Fat Paulie bet me fifty bucks he
could eat more hot dogs than me.

11:28.454 --> 11:31.178
He knocked off twenty four.
Guy's an animal.

11:31.314 --> 11:32.658
Are you crazy?

11:32.682 --> 11:34.224
You lost fifty dollars?

11:34.248 --> 11:36.604
Dolores. Please.

11:38.248 --> 11:40.049
I ate twenty six.

11:44.882 --> 11:46.590
You're so lucky.

11:46.616 --> 11:47.879
You know that?

11:48.319 --> 11:50.574
Rent is due on Monday.

11:55.466 --> 11:57.736
You're gonna get that?

11:58.990 --> 12:00.116
Yeah?

12:00.140 --> 12:04.819
Hey Lip. Some guy called over here, a
doctor. He's looking for a driver.

12:05.140 --> 12:06.957
- You interested?
- Yeah.

12:06.981 --> 12:09.642
They're interviewing
guys tomorrow afternoon.

12:09.789 --> 12:12.114
The address is...

12:12.193 --> 12:16.213
Eight eighty one, 7th avenue, two fifteen.

12:36.471 --> 12:37.671
Hey!

12:37.893 --> 12:39.898
- Excuse me.
- We're not open right now. But you're

12:39.922 --> 12:42.086
welcome to buy tickets to
tonight's performance.

12:42.125 --> 12:44.234
Nah. That's not it.

12:44.258 --> 12:48.477
I think I got the wrong address.
But is there a doctor's office in here?

12:48.547 --> 12:50.122
A doctor's office?

12:50.290 --> 12:51.580
- Dr Shirley.

12:51.604 --> 12:55.280
You have the correct address. Dr Shirley
lives upstairs, above the hall.

13:01.468 --> 13:03.160
How you doing?

13:14.013 --> 13:17.646
I'm here for the driver job.
Tony Lip.

13:19.587 --> 13:21.686
No Tony Lip.

13:21.840 --> 13:23.665
No it should be on there.

13:26.488 --> 13:28.434
No... Um...

13:28.458 --> 13:32.643
- I have a Tony Val... Valle...
- Vallelonga. Yeah, that's me.

13:35.129 --> 13:37.258
- Fill it out while you wait.
- What?

13:37.792 --> 13:39.648
Fill it out while you wait.

14:04.098 --> 14:05.689
Have a seat.

14:33.331 --> 14:36.211
Mr. Vallelonga, sorry to keep you
waiting.

14:39.266 --> 14:40.794
I'm Dr. Donald Shirley.

14:41.344 --> 14:44.498
- Tony.
- Yes. Please sit down.

14:48.320 --> 14:50.606
Some place you got in here.

14:51.148 --> 14:53.082
Them horns real?

14:53.328 --> 14:55.043
Elephant tusks. Yes.

14:56.707 --> 14:58.180
What about that?

14:58.183 --> 14:59.688
That a molar?

15:01.261 --> 15:03.133
- A what?
- A molar.

15:03.231 --> 15:04.830
Like a Shark tooth?

15:05.094 --> 15:07.195
Tiger's maybe.

15:07.219 --> 15:08.794
It was a gift.

15:09.457 --> 15:12.524
I thought, I thought I
was going to a office.

15:12.707 --> 15:15.298
They said a doctor needed a driver.

15:15.762 --> 15:17.243
That's all they told you?

15:17.269 --> 15:20.571
- Yeah.
- Actually, it's a bit more complicated than that.

15:22.500 --> 15:24.934
Have you ever driven
professionally before?

15:26.121 --> 15:29.149
Sanitation. Garbage trucks.

15:29.848 --> 15:33.470
Plus I drive my boss home at night.
But I can drive anything.

15:33.770 --> 15:35.751
Limos, tow trucks.

15:36.033 --> 15:37.665
Snow palms, whatever.

15:37.689 --> 15:40.736
I see. What other
experience do you have?

15:40.760 --> 15:44.666
I worked a lot of joints. The Wagon
Wheel, Peppermint Lounge, Copa

15:44.690 --> 15:47.226
- In what capacity?
- What do you mean?

15:47.979 --> 15:50.960
- What did you do there?
- Ah...

15:52.296 --> 15:54.090
Public relations.

15:55.018 --> 15:59.327
Well, first of all, Tony, I'm not a
medical doctor. I'm a musician.

15:59.586 --> 16:02.506
- You mean like songs?
- Yes.

16:02.530 --> 16:06.581
I'm about to embark on a concert tour, the
majority of which will be down South.

16:06.586 --> 16:08.887
- Atlantic city?
- No.

16:09.113 --> 16:14.032
The deep south. First we're starting in the
Midwest, but then we're taking a hard left.

16:14.244 --> 16:17.608
Kentucky, North Carolina, Tennessee,
and on down through the Delta.

16:17.971 --> 16:20.984
Do you foresee any issues in working
for a black man?

16:21.674 --> 16:22.905
No!

16:23.560 --> 16:26.476
No no. Just the other
day me and the wife had

16:26.500 --> 16:29.487
a couple of colored
guys over at the house.

16:30.569 --> 16:32.472
For drinks.

16:32.983 --> 16:35.222
Hmm. I see, you're married.

16:35.433 --> 16:37.844
Yeah. Two kids.

16:39.640 --> 16:42.455
I am not sure this is the proper
job for a married man.

16:42.479 --> 16:44.234
Why, we bringing broads?

16:45.025 --> 16:47.410
My point is, you'll be
gone for eight straight

16:47.434 --> 16:49.866
weeks, no breaks, right
up until Christmas.

16:50.723 --> 16:53.259
You're quite sure you can leave
your family for that long?

16:53.360 --> 16:54.714
Depends on what you're paying.

16:54.738 --> 16:57.326
A hundred dollars a week,
plus room and board.

16:58.015 --> 17:02.614
But let me be crystal clear... I'm
not just hiring a chauffeur.

17:03.052 --> 17:07.971
I need someone who can handle my itinerary.
Be a personal assistant. I need a valet.

17:08.148 --> 17:12.497
I need someone who can launder
my clothes, shine my shoes...

17:14.251 --> 17:15.771
Good luck, Doc.

17:18.781 --> 17:20.035
Tony.

17:25.294 --> 17:28.447
I had my record label ask around
town to find me the right man.

17:29.060 --> 17:31.174
Your name came up more than once.

17:32.214 --> 17:37.663
You've impressed several people with
your... innate ability to handle trouble.

17:38.968 --> 17:42.371
And that is why I called and
inquired about your availability.

17:45.950 --> 17:49.259
OK, here is the deal. I got no
problem being on a road with you.

17:49.578 --> 17:50.958
But I ain't no butler.

17:51.054 --> 17:53.972
I ain't ironing no shirts, and I'm
not polishing nobody's shoes.

17:53.996 --> 17:56.815
You need someone to get you from point
A to point B? You need someone to make

17:56.839 --> 18:00.523
sure there's no problems along the way...
And believe me you in the deep South

18:00.966 --> 18:02.440
there's gonna be problems.

18:03.326 --> 18:06.216
So if you want me, it's a
buck and a quarter a week.

18:06.240 --> 18:07.759
Or go hire the little
Chink that just

18:07.783 --> 18:09.660
pranced out of here,
see how far you get.

18:12.647 --> 18:14.409
Well, Mr. Vallelonga.

18:15.894 --> 18:17.578
Thank you for stopping by.

18:30.487 --> 18:31.734
Hey Bobby.

18:32.186 --> 18:33.949
Give me a Rheingold.

18:34.047 --> 18:35.771
Ice cold.

18:44.543 --> 18:46.649
Mr Tony.

18:47.504 --> 18:49.173
Augie asking about you.

18:50.336 --> 18:54.942
- Come on, I'm dying of thirst over here!
- Shut up. I'm talking.

18:58.797 --> 19:00.341
- When?
- Now.

19:00.664 --> 19:02.497
He in his box.

19:28.174 --> 19:29.976
Tony Lip.

19:30.822 --> 19:32.647
What the hell happened at
the Copa?

19:32.826 --> 19:34.932
I heard you split a guy's
face open.

19:36.268 --> 19:38.905
That guy you hit. Mickey Charon.

19:39.004 --> 19:41.158
Charlie the Hand's crew.

19:41.742 --> 19:43.458
Guess he shoulda known better.

19:48.564 --> 19:50.381
Hand asked me to look into it.

19:50.580 --> 19:54.201
I spoke to Podell.
Whole thing was a...

19:54.204 --> 19:56.506
over a piece of ass, right?

19:56.923 --> 19:58.138
Yeah.

19:58.684 --> 20:03.931
Beef like that should never happen
inside the club. They were out of line.

20:04.733 --> 20:06.589
So we squashed it.

20:08.836 --> 20:11.338
You looking to earn a
little extra scharole?

20:11.362 --> 20:13.896
I can keep you busy
while the Copa's down.

20:14.926 --> 20:16.595
What I gotta do?

20:17.825 --> 20:19.321
Things...

20:22.590 --> 20:26.908
Appreciate it, but I'm gonna spend
some time with the family.

20:27.059 --> 20:30.263
Don't be stupid. You make
yourself a few extra bucks, buy

20:30.287 --> 20:33.635
something nice for that pretty
little your wife of yours.

20:38.201 --> 20:41.409
Nah, I'm good. I'm
flushed right now.

20:55.246 --> 21:00.415
Here's fifty. Pay me sixty by
New Year, you get it back.

21:03.045 --> 21:07.065
Hey Lip. Everything OK?

21:07.987 --> 21:10.187
What? You got beak trouble Charlie?

21:10.885 --> 21:12.584
Mind your business.

21:16.298 --> 21:20.103
So come on. Dying to hear what
happened with the doctor interview?

21:20.127 --> 21:23.577
He ain't a real doctor, he's a
piano player.

21:23.963 --> 21:27.467
But I don't understand, why'd
they say that he was a doctor?

21:27.500 --> 21:31.414
I don't know. I think he's like a
doctor of piano-playing or something.

21:31.438 --> 21:32.985
You can be that?

21:33.009 --> 21:36.592
I guess. He lives on
top of Carnegie Hall.

21:36.823 --> 21:38.962
You shoulda seen this place, Dee.
It was filled

21:38.986 --> 21:41.208
with statues and all
kinds of fancy crap.

21:41.227 --> 21:43.812
And he was sitting on top
of a friggin' throne all

21:43.836 --> 21:46.467
dressed up like the king
of the jungle bunnies.

21:46.918 --> 21:48.439
He's colored?

21:51.492 --> 21:55.520
- Then you wouldn't last a week with him.
- For right money, I would.

22:06.118 --> 22:07.318
Yeah.

22:08.485 --> 22:09.685
Oh.

22:10.321 --> 22:12.131
Look. Uh...

22:12.446 --> 22:13.928
Really?

22:15.177 --> 22:17.439
OK. OK. Hold on a sec.

22:17.919 --> 22:20.235
It's Dr Shirley.

22:20.259 --> 22:22.514
The Piano guy, he
wants to talk to you.

22:23.322 --> 22:25.100
- Me?
- Yeah.

22:25.103 --> 22:26.865
What? No!

22:27.036 --> 22:29.197
Come here. Take it.

22:29.848 --> 22:31.563
Just talk.

22:34.365 --> 22:35.604
Hello.

22:37.826 --> 22:40.924
Good morning, Doctor,
it's nice to talk to you.

22:46.137 --> 22:48.758
Yes, that is a long time...

22:51.343 --> 22:52.808
It is.

22:55.132 --> 22:56.973
Yes. I'm sure.

22:58.991 --> 23:02.175
Thank you for calling...
Bye now.

23:06.142 --> 23:07.412
What did he say?

23:08.205 --> 23:11.079
He wanted to know if I'd
be okay with him taking

23:11.103 --> 23:14.116
my husband away from his
family for two months.

23:15.698 --> 23:17.906
He said he'd pay you
what you asked for.

23:23.815 --> 23:25.030
- Hey!
- Uh huh?

23:27.229 --> 23:28.741
It's good money.

23:29.081 --> 23:30.632
We need it.

23:33.352 --> 23:37.154
I can't be eatin' twenty six
hot dogs every day.

23:38.949 --> 23:40.297
I know.

23:41.223 --> 23:44.173
I told him it was okay
for you to go.

23:46.520 --> 23:49.006
Alright. Hey look. Here's
the first half of your pay.

23:49.030 --> 23:51.070
You're gonna get the rest
when the tour's over.

23:51.099 --> 23:52.536
- I gotta get paid every week.
- Sorry,

23:52.560 --> 23:54.400
that's not how the
record company does it.

23:54.661 --> 23:57.187
We gotta have some guarantee
you're gonna finish the job.

23:57.211 --> 23:59.979
Why wouldn't I finish the job?
I took it, didn't I?

24:00.594 --> 24:02.817
Well, then we got nothing to worry about.

24:03.563 --> 24:06.193
Here's the deal, Mr. Vallelonga.

24:06.220 --> 24:08.314
OK! It's your job to get
Don to all his tour

24:08.338 --> 24:10.336
dates on time. Now if
he misses any shows,

24:10.360 --> 24:12.867
- you're not getting your back-end.
- He's not gonna miss any show.

24:12.891 --> 24:15.646
Good. Oh, you're gonna need this.

24:16.799 --> 24:18.933
Now this is the book I was
telling you about. Sometimes you

24:18.957 --> 24:21.397
guys are staying in the same
hotel, sometimes you're not.

24:22.553 --> 24:26.471
- Oh yeah, I do...
- Yeah, don't let me down. Let's go.

24:35.453 --> 24:39.215
- Is this the new one?
- Yeah. The record company rented it.

24:39.351 --> 24:41.153
- Nice huh.
- Beautiful.

24:41.349 --> 24:44.328
So what my sister have to say about
you being gone for three weeks?

24:44.352 --> 24:46.122
Eight weeks.

24:46.553 --> 24:50.346
Ten-to-one, you slap this moolie
out, you come home in under a month.

24:52.507 --> 24:54.367
- Hi boys.
- Say goodbye to your father.

24:54.391 --> 24:55.872
Frankie, Nicky, come here.

24:56.726 --> 24:58.960
- Hi, will you be good boys?
- Uh huh.

24:58.984 --> 25:00.653
- Listen to your mother?
- Uh huh.

25:01.112 --> 25:04.065
Alright, give me a kiss.
I'm counting on you on this.

25:05.534 --> 25:07.429
- Don't go too far.
- We won't.

25:11.038 --> 25:13.976
- Did you go to the A-A-A for the maps?
- Yes, no. I mean

25:14.000 --> 25:17.747
the record company gave me maps and
the itinerary and this thing.

25:19.920 --> 25:21.919
The Negro Motorist Green-Book?

25:21.943 --> 25:25.690
Yeah it lists all places coloreds can
stay down south. Like, you know,

25:25.732 --> 25:27.370
traveling while black.

25:27.433 --> 25:28.816
Traveling while black?

25:28.840 --> 25:31.714
Yeah. If you're black and you
gotta travel for some reason.

25:31.738 --> 25:33.316
They had a special book for that?

25:33.340 --> 25:34.808
I guess.

25:34.832 --> 25:36.167
Did you pack the iron?

25:36.191 --> 25:38.800
- I ain't lugging no iron, Dee.
- How're you gonna press your pants?

25:38.824 --> 25:40.501
I'll put 'em under the mattress.

25:41.807 --> 25:43.921
I want you to write me a letter

25:43.924 --> 25:46.616
- every chance you get.
- I can't write letters.

25:46.847 --> 25:48.682
- Yes, you can.
- I can't write.

25:48.706 --> 25:50.761
- Take you five minutes. Promise me.
- It's embarrassing.

25:50.785 --> 25:52.018
They ain't gonna be no good.

25:52.042 --> 25:54.586
It's a lot cheaper than calling
long distance, Tony.

25:55.081 --> 25:56.953
Promise me you're gonna write.

25:57.183 --> 25:58.383
I promise.

26:00.466 --> 26:02.924
Here... Put this in the bank today.

26:02.943 --> 26:04.455
It's half my pay.

26:04.479 --> 26:08.265
Oh, here is a couple of
sandwiches for you and Dr. Shirley.

26:08.721 --> 26:09.861
Thanks.

26:09.885 --> 26:11.632
- Be careful.
- I will.

26:12.002 --> 26:15.553
- I love you.
- I love you too, baby.

26:19.220 --> 26:23.311
You better be home for Christmas or
don't come home at all!

26:27.530 --> 26:30.159
I got it pop. I got it.

26:56.790 --> 26:59.029
Hey! I'm Tony.

26:59.456 --> 27:01.875
The driver.
Bum a smoke?

27:07.392 --> 27:08.897
Thanks.

27:18.031 --> 27:19.555
So, you're with the band?

27:21.512 --> 27:23.368
Oleg. Cello.

27:24.083 --> 27:25.348
George. Bass.

27:25.372 --> 27:28.009
And we're not a band,
we're a trio.

27:28.348 --> 27:29.845
Oh, a trio?

27:30.098 --> 27:31.219
Right.

27:31.243 --> 27:34.302
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

27:58.973 --> 28:00.415
Thank you, Amit.

28:01.796 --> 28:03.493
Have a wonderful trip, Sir.

29:12.188 --> 29:15.218
Tony, the first thing I'd like you
to do, when we arrive in the city,

29:15.242 --> 29:19.466
is check the piano where I'm playing, make
sure it's a Steinway as per my contract.

29:22.589 --> 29:26.016
And can you see to it that there is
a bottle of Cutty Sark in my room

29:26.261 --> 29:27.688
every night.

29:28.160 --> 29:29.750
Every night?

29:31.169 --> 29:33.906
Well if you ever need
any help with that...

29:33.930 --> 29:35.130
I won't.

29:37.417 --> 29:39.492
Ten-and-two on the
wheel, please.

29:42.687 --> 29:44.019
Hey Doc.

29:44.296 --> 29:46.551
I noticed on the itinerary thing,

29:46.780 --> 29:49.225
last show's on the 23rd December.

29:49.249 --> 29:51.977
- Right?
- Birmingham, yes. It's a Christmas show.

29:52.001 --> 29:54.347
So, any way we could maybe
hit the road early next

29:54.371 --> 29:57.039
morning so we could be home
in time for Christmas Eve?

29:57.063 --> 29:58.458
We'll see.

29:58.501 --> 30:00.224
Appreciate it.

30:01.501 --> 30:03.349
Could you put out the cigarette please?

30:03.594 --> 30:04.865
Why?

30:05.323 --> 30:07.195
I can't breath back here.

30:10.090 --> 30:13.785
What are you talking about? Smoke's going
into my lungs. I'm doing all the work here.

30:13.809 --> 30:15.101
Thank you.

31:07.727 --> 31:09.177
What are you looking at?

31:11.313 --> 31:13.903
- You speak German, huh?
- That was Russian.

31:14.366 --> 31:16.959
Yeah, I was stationed in Germany in
the army.

31:16.983 --> 31:19.441
I can pick up a little bit of
what you're saying there.

31:19.608 --> 31:21.878
Watch out for them Krauts.

31:22.093 --> 31:23.824
They're all snakes.

31:23.944 --> 31:26.371
Kennedy shoulda bombed 'em
when he had the chance.

31:26.468 --> 31:28.566
Plus now them Cuban bastards.

31:30.093 --> 31:32.574
Ain't they supposed
to be following us?

31:33.014 --> 31:35.315
They have the itinerary. As
long as they get to the show

31:35.339 --> 31:38.239
on time, I am not worried about
it and neither should you.

31:39.305 --> 31:40.990
I ain't worried about nothing.

31:42.469 --> 31:44.977
Fact, when you see me worried, you'll know.

31:45.001 --> 31:47.802
- You'll know if I'm worried.
- Tony. How about some quite time?

31:49.383 --> 31:50.591
Sure.

31:54.204 --> 31:56.217
It's amazing you said that.

31:56.532 --> 31:58.467
How about some quite time?

31:58.955 --> 32:00.567
Dolores, my wife, she
used to say that all

32:00.591 --> 32:02.511
time, well not all the
time, but you know...

32:02.749 --> 32:04.431
She says it when I come
off from work some time,

32:04.455 --> 32:06.191
you know, she's been with
the kids all that day.

32:06.215 --> 32:08.923
And she would say, Tony...
How about some quite time?

32:08.934 --> 32:10.767
Exactly like how you said it.

32:10.840 --> 32:12.345
It means... amazing.

32:19.483 --> 32:20.917
How was that?

32:22.538 --> 32:23.902
Salty.

32:26.661 --> 32:29.228
Have you ever considered
becoming a food critic?

32:31.806 --> 32:34.037
No... Not really.

32:34.165 --> 32:35.629
Why? Is there money in it?

32:35.653 --> 32:40.103
I'm just saying, you have a marvelous
way with words when describing food.

32:40.973 --> 32:42.368
SALTY!

32:43.112 --> 32:45.515
So vivid. One can
almost taste it.

32:46.643 --> 32:48.882
I'm saying it's salty.

32:48.893 --> 32:50.496
And salt's cheating.

32:50.520 --> 32:52.611
Any cook can make things salty.
But to make it taste

32:52.635 --> 32:54.845
good without the salt, with
just the other flavors

32:54.949 --> 32:56.235
that's the trick.

32:56.575 --> 33:00.705
We should really get going soon if we
expect to get to Pittsburgh by dinner.

33:02.060 --> 33:03.637
When I was in the army

33:03.661 --> 33:05.447
I knew a guy from Pittsburgh

33:05.969 --> 33:08.130
except he called it Tits-burgh

33:08.200 --> 33:11.275
he said
all the women there have huge tits.

33:12.825 --> 33:14.174
That's absurd.

33:14.242 --> 33:18.472
Why would women in Pittsburgh have larger
breasts than, say, women in New York?

33:18.496 --> 33:20.579
Guess we'll find out, huh?

33:23.028 --> 33:24.806
You know, when you
first hired me

33:25.270 --> 33:28.728
my wife went out bought one of your
records, one about the orphans.

33:29.723 --> 33:31.017
Orphans?

33:31.690 --> 33:35.406
Yeah. Cover had a bunch of kids
sitting around a campfire?

33:36.227 --> 33:37.857
Orpheus.

33:39.489 --> 33:40.326
Yeah.

33:40.350 --> 33:43.057
Orpheus in the Underworld.
It's based on a French Opera.

33:43.685 --> 33:45.830
And those weren't
children on the cover.

33:46.161 --> 33:48.447
Those were demon in the bowels of hell.

33:49.325 --> 33:52.400
No shit. Must have
been naughty kids.

34:07.575 --> 34:10.939
- What are you doing?
- I gotta take a leak. Doc.

34:11.779 --> 34:15.127
- Here? Now?
- You want me to piss my pants?

35:33.937 --> 35:36.723
Oh hey Doc, good afternoon.

35:37.067 --> 35:39.759
Take this for any
incidentals we may need.

35:40.427 --> 35:44.209
If you want to buy something, you don't
have to ask, just keep the receipt please.

35:44.233 --> 35:46.042
When it runs low let me know.

35:46.381 --> 35:47.886
Oh, thanks.

35:47.905 --> 35:49.941
One more thing.

35:51.032 --> 35:55.100
We will be attending many events
before and after the concerts

35:55.167 --> 35:58.922
interacting with some of the wealthiest and
most highly-educated people in the country.

35:59.509 --> 36:01.927
It is my feeling
that your diction

36:02.171 --> 36:05.597
however charming it may be in the
tri-state area, could use some

36:05.882 --> 36:07.173
finessing.

36:07.197 --> 36:10.538
You mean diction,
like in what way?

36:11.408 --> 36:14.162
Like in the only way the word is ever used.

36:14.879 --> 36:15.979
Okay.

36:16.003 --> 36:18.962
Your intonation, inflection,
your choice of words.

36:19.927 --> 36:22.038
I got my own problems,
now I gotta worry about

36:22.062 --> 36:24.004
what people think
about the way I talk?

36:24.028 --> 36:27.456
There are simple techniques I can teach you
that are quite effective. I can help you.

36:27.480 --> 36:29.241
I don't need no goddamn help.

36:29.265 --> 36:31.832
People don't like the way I talk,
they can go take a shit.

36:32.897 --> 36:37.201
- The profanity is another issue.
- A fanabla, why you breaking my balls?

36:37.225 --> 36:39.464
Because you can do better. Mr Vallelonga.

36:39.785 --> 36:41.837
Which brings me
to one more point

36:41.883 --> 36:44.711
as the guest of honor, I will
be introduced when entering

36:44.735 --> 36:47.614
these intimate events. You
will be introduced as well.

36:47.923 --> 36:50.045
In my humble opinion

36:50.259 --> 36:52.829
Vallelonga may be difficult to
pronounce.

36:52.853 --> 36:55.326
So, I was thinking...

36:55.357 --> 36:58.408
Valle would be more appropriate.
Tony Valle.

36:58.458 --> 37:00.088
Short and sweet.

37:01.163 --> 37:02.395
Nah!

37:02.796 --> 37:05.637
If they got a problem with
Vallelonga, they can call me Tony Lip.

37:05.642 --> 37:09.866
These are genteel people. Tony Lip might
be a little...

37:10.494 --> 37:12.163
worldly for them.

37:12.312 --> 37:14.567
Well, then it's Tony Vallelonga.

37:14.912 --> 37:18.500
All these high-class people, so much
smarter than me, with their intelligence

37:18.524 --> 37:22.034
and speaking abilities, you're telling
me they can't pronounce my name?

37:22.404 --> 37:25.564
They don't like it, they can shove it
up their ass, I'll just wait outside.

37:27.107 --> 37:29.260
That sound compromised.

37:45.610 --> 37:47.989
Ladies and gentlemen,
tonight we are

37:48.013 --> 37:51.232
privileged to present a
great American artist.

37:51.828 --> 37:55.504
He gave his first public
performance at the age of three.

37:55.608 --> 37:58.989
At age eighteen, at Arthur
Fiedler's invitation, our

37:59.013 --> 38:02.782
guest made his concert
debut with the Boston Pops.

38:02.897 --> 38:08.418
He holds Doctorates in Psychology,
in Music, and in the Liturgical Arts

38:08.423 --> 38:12.530
and he had performed at the White House
twice in the past fourteen months.

38:12.554 --> 38:14.973
He is a true virtuoso.

38:15.129 --> 38:18.829
Virtuoso... that's Italian.

38:20.074 --> 38:22.719
Means he's really good.

38:23.873 --> 38:28.174
So Ladies and gentleman, please
welcome The Don Shirley Trio!

40:08.281 --> 40:11.292
Hey, it's your dice, I'm just
having a lucky night.

40:11.316 --> 40:12.516
Tony.

40:13.918 --> 40:15.781
Boss man's calling.

40:15.805 --> 40:18.044
He ain't my boss. I work
for the record company.

40:18.050 --> 40:20.156
I work for the record company too.

40:20.425 --> 40:23.432
Come on man! Give us a
chance to win back our loot!

40:23.456 --> 40:25.133
I'm sorry, fellas, duty calls!

40:25.441 --> 40:27.367
Duty calls?

40:27.392 --> 40:29.694
Look man, my duty is
getting my money back.

40:30.005 --> 40:31.506
I've been looking for you.

40:31.530 --> 40:34.082
Yeah sorry. The guys were
having a little game.

40:34.565 --> 40:37.109
Next time you need extra
money, you just ask me.

40:37.604 --> 40:39.695
More fun winning it.

40:39.776 --> 40:41.460
Then what if you lost?

40:41.784 --> 40:43.932
Craps and cards, I don't lose, Doc.

40:43.956 --> 40:45.398
I don't lose.

40:46.495 --> 40:50.249
So stooping down in the gravel pitching
dice for pocket change makes you a winner?

40:51.221 --> 40:53.796
What are you giving me shit for?
Everybody was doing it.

40:53.839 --> 40:56.648
They didn't have a choice
whether to be inside or out.

40:58.089 --> 40:59.398
You did.

41:02.538 --> 41:04.910
And wipe off your knees,
you have dirt on them.

41:25.317 --> 41:29.799
Dear Dolores... How are you?
I am fine...

41:30.029 --> 41:33.378
I'm eating real
good, hamburgers mostly

41:33.576 --> 41:36.120
so don't worry about me not
eating good.

41:36.554 --> 41:40.332
I saw Dr. Shirley
play the piano. Tonight.

41:40.742 --> 41:45.356
He doesn't play like a colored guy.
He plays like Liberace but better.

41:46.289 --> 41:48.466
He's like a genius I think.

41:48.514 --> 41:50.904
When I look at him in the
rear-view mirror, I can

41:50.928 --> 41:53.599
tell he's always thinking
about stuff in his head.

41:53.623 --> 41:56.163
I guess that's what geniuses do.

41:56.187 --> 41:58.645
But it don't look
fun to be that smart.

41:59.507 --> 42:02.567
I miss you very very much.

42:11.848 --> 42:14.473
- Who is this?
- Who?

42:14.497 --> 42:16.298
On the radio?

42:16.603 --> 42:18.342
Lil' Richard.

42:18.872 --> 42:21.372
Really? That's Little Richard?

42:21.396 --> 42:24.322
Yeah. Think you could
play something like this, Doc?

42:26.270 --> 42:28.689
I don't know. Sounds
very complicated.

42:29.176 --> 42:30.978
Ain't that right.

42:32.117 --> 42:34.473
So where did this “Tony
the Lip” moniker come from?

42:35.873 --> 42:37.938
It's not Tony the Lip.

42:37.962 --> 42:40.022
It's Tony Lip.
One word.

42:40.046 --> 42:42.154
I got it when I was a kid.
Because my friends

42:42.178 --> 42:44.754
said I was the best bullshit
artist in the Bronx.

42:45.728 --> 42:48.698
- Why are you smiling?
- What do you mean?

42:49.537 --> 42:51.584
It doesn't bother you
that your friends, the

42:51.608 --> 42:53.808
people closest to you,
consider you a liar?

42:53.819 --> 42:57.208
Who said liar?
I said bullshit artist.

42:57.232 --> 43:01.018
- Then what's the difference?
- Cause I don't lie. Ever.

43:01.396 --> 43:05.534
I'm just good at talking people into, you
know, doing things they don't wanna do.

43:05.600 --> 43:07.245
By bulletin 'em.

43:07.865 --> 43:10.019
And you're proud of that?

43:10.043 --> 43:12.181
Well it got me this job.

43:17.181 --> 43:20.557
Wait a minute. You're full of shit!
You never heard of Chubby Checker?

43:20.581 --> 43:23.840
Of course I've heard of him,
I just never heard his music before.

43:23.925 --> 43:26.367
But I like this. This is nice.

43:27.422 --> 43:30.044
He's got a silky voice...
very smooth.

43:30.192 --> 43:32.256
This is what everybody
is dancing to now.

43:32.280 --> 43:33.854
Eyes on the road Tony.

43:36.853 --> 43:38.499
You know this song?

43:38.934 --> 43:42.603
- I don't think so. No.
- How could you not know this music?

43:42.673 --> 43:44.178
Aretha Frank.

43:45.087 --> 43:47.726
Chubby Checker, Lil' Richard, Sam
Cooke.

43:47.750 --> 43:51.207
Come on Doc, these
are your people!

44:05.078 --> 44:08.450
- You want anything? I'm gonna pack smoke.
- No thank you.

44:42.215 --> 44:44.814
Nice turn Mike, what he makes it up?

44:47.799 --> 44:49.655
Snatch an apple Doc.

44:55.406 --> 44:58.035
Before we pull out Tony,
we need to have a talk.

45:00.278 --> 45:02.697
- Yeah?
- Oleg told me what you did.

45:02.892 --> 45:04.207
What I do?

45:04.231 --> 45:06.634
You stole a jade
stone from the store.

45:06.719 --> 45:08.695
- No I didn't.
- He watched you do it.

45:08.719 --> 45:10.482
I didn't steal no stone.

45:10.576 --> 45:12.558
You picked it up and you
put it in your pocket.

45:12.582 --> 45:15.565
I picked up a rock up off the ground.
I didn't steal from the box.

45:15.589 --> 45:17.608
Now why would you
pick up a rock off the ground?

45:17.632 --> 45:19.215
I don't know.

45:19.957 --> 45:22.675
'Cause that ain't stealing.
Just a regular rock.

45:22.699 --> 45:24.860
And why would you
want a regular rock?

45:25.316 --> 45:26.635
To have.

45:26.659 --> 45:28.873
- For luck maybe.
- A lucky rock.

45:28.897 --> 45:31.003
- Yeah.
- Let me see it.

45:45.491 --> 45:47.512
Take it back and pay for it.

45:49.735 --> 45:53.725
I told you that Kraut was a sneak. Rats
me out for something I didn't even do.

45:53.918 --> 45:55.769
Pay for the stone, Tony,
you'll feel better.

45:55.793 --> 45:56.837
I feel fine.

45:56.861 --> 46:00.280
And I ain't paying for no
regular rock I found in the dirt.

46:00.821 --> 46:03.354
Do not drive, Mr. Vallelonga.

46:07.091 --> 46:08.635
Put it back.

46:32.609 --> 46:35.121
- You feel better?
- No.

46:35.499 --> 46:38.225
If you'd like, Tony, I would happily
buy you that stone.

46:38.249 --> 46:40.980
Don't bother. You took
all the fun out of it.

47:18.350 --> 47:20.050
Excuse me, Sir.

47:21.217 --> 47:23.472
- I'm with the band.
- You're all set up.

47:23.627 --> 47:26.507
- This isn't the piano, right?
- That's it.

47:26.916 --> 47:28.452
It ain't a Steinway.

47:29.424 --> 47:30.588
So what?

47:30.612 --> 47:34.835
Dr. Shirley only plays on Steinway-brand
pianos. It's in his written contract.

47:35.328 --> 47:37.991
- Who's Dr. Shirley?
- Dr. Shirley...

47:38.015 --> 47:39.571
the Don Shirley Trio?

47:39.595 --> 47:40.864
They're playing tonight.

47:40.885 --> 47:44.796
- Does it really matter?
- Yeah, it does, to this contract.

47:46.432 --> 47:50.616
Come on man, these coons can play on
anything you put in front of them.

47:54.635 --> 47:56.417
But it's a piece of shit.

47:56.441 --> 47:57.936
And there is garbage in there.

47:57.996 --> 48:01.360
- So, take it out.
- What'd you say?

48:02.930 --> 48:04.607
You heard me.

48:07.692 --> 48:11.895
Hey, you got 2-3 hours.
Just get a clean Steinway in here.

48:11.919 --> 48:15.197
- There ain't no Steinway on campus.
- Not my problem.

48:15.532 --> 48:18.388
I bet there is not two Steinway
in the whole state of Indiana.

48:18.625 --> 48:20.755
I guess you better
move your ass then.

48:20.805 --> 48:22.885
Who do you think you're
talking to, grease ball?

48:52.672 --> 48:57.881
Dear Dolores... This morning I had
steak and eggs. For breakfast.

48:57.905 --> 49:01.784
The band has been playing at very
ritzy joints.

49:01.912 --> 49:05.363
Dr. Shirley and I are getting
along pretty good, but sometimes

49:05.387 --> 49:08.953
I think he gets sad and
that's why he drinks too much.

49:09.492 --> 49:14.630
I never knew how very beautiful this
country was. Now that I'm seeing it I know.

49:15.321 --> 49:20.232
You wouldn't believe how beautiful nature
is, it is as beautiful as they say.

49:20.373 --> 49:24.245
And the traffic out here in the country
is nothing, which is fine by me.

49:24.882 --> 49:27.504
“Right now I'm eating
spaghetti and meatballs in a

49:27.528 --> 49:30.348
diner that tastes like
ketchup on Chinese noodles.

49:30.932 --> 49:33.856
“We are heading down south now...
I will write you

49:33.880 --> 49:36.945
another letter when we get down south.
I love you.

49:37.199 --> 49:40.985
- Your husband Tony. P.S.
- Kiss the kids for me.

49:49.709 --> 49:51.411
You got any family, Doc?

49:51.435 --> 49:53.632
- Not really.
- Not really?

49:53.656 --> 49:55.534
Either you do or you don't.

49:56.656 --> 49:58.808
It's a long story, Tony.

49:58.832 --> 50:00.751
What, we're in a hurry now?

50:02.670 --> 50:04.175
Let's hear it.

50:05.192 --> 50:07.439
I have a brother somewhere.

50:08.297 --> 50:10.595
We used to get together
once in a while... but it

50:10.619 --> 50:12.975
got more and more
difficult to stay in touch.

50:13.415 --> 50:15.896
Curse of being a musician I guess.

50:16.633 --> 50:18.689
Always on the road

50:18.713 --> 50:20.515
like a carnival worker.

50:21.669 --> 50:23.479
Or a criminal.

50:23.631 --> 50:26.065
Took quite a toll on my marriage as
well.

50:26.186 --> 50:28.295
- You're married?
- Was.

50:28.319 --> 50:32.081
June, good person.

50:32.089 --> 50:34.376
Terrible grammar,
but a kind soul.

50:34.400 --> 50:36.920
- You'll quite like her.
- June?

50:37.345 --> 50:39.522
Like month?

50:41.542 --> 50:45.883
Unfortunately, I couldn't do a
husband act and a concert pianist act.

50:46.901 --> 50:49.671
Couldn't seem to manage both worlds.

50:51.594 --> 50:53.490
Kentucky Fried Chicken.

50:53.613 --> 50:56.970
In Kentucky! When's
that ever gonna happen?!

51:11.611 --> 51:15.592
- Hey, you want some?
- I'm fine. Thank you Tony.

51:18.366 --> 51:22.676
I think this is the best Kentucky
Fried Chicken I ever had.

51:23.078 --> 51:24.984
But I guess it's fresher
down here, right?

51:25.008 --> 51:27.449
I don't think I've ever met
anyone with your appetite.

51:27.473 --> 51:30.067
No, I bought the bucket
so you could have some.

51:30.091 --> 51:32.721
I've never had fried
chicken in my life.

51:33.484 --> 51:38.599
Who you bulletin? You people love the fried
chicken, the grits, the colored greens

51:39.398 --> 51:40.546
I love it, too.

51:40.570 --> 51:43.391
The negro cooks used to make
it all time when I was in the army.

51:43.415 --> 51:46.138
You have a very narrow
assessment of me, Tony.

51:46.299 --> 51:48.139
Yeah right? I'm good.

51:48.286 --> 51:51.408
No, you're not good, you're bad.

51:51.564 --> 51:54.354
I'm saying, just because other Negros
enjoy certain types of music, it

51:54.378 --> 51:57.968
doesn't mean I have to. Nor do we
all have to eat the same kind food.

51:58.965 --> 52:03.449
Wait a minute. If you said all guineas
like pizza and spaghetti and meatballs

52:03.473 --> 52:05.990
- I'm not gonna get insulted.
- Well, you're missing the point.

52:06.014 --> 52:08.084
For you to make the
assumption that every Negro...

52:08.108 --> 52:10.182
- Hey, you want some or not?
- No.

52:10.225 --> 52:11.839
Here. Come on.

52:11.878 --> 52:15.643
- Tell me that don't smell good?
- It smells okay

52:15.667 --> 52:18.598
I prefer not to
get grease on my blanket.

52:18.622 --> 52:22.537
Ooh, I'm gonna get grease on my blankie.
Come on, have a piece.

52:22.561 --> 52:24.428
It ain't gonna kill ya.
Come on. Take it easy.

52:24.452 --> 52:25.674
- No.
- Take it.

52:25.878 --> 52:28.190
- I'm gonna throw it in the back.
- Don't you dare.

52:28.214 --> 52:31.640
- Then you better take it.
- How? Do you have plates? Or utensils?

52:31.664 --> 52:33.120
Bah fongool! Eat it
with your hands,

52:33.144 --> 52:35.136
- that's how you're supposed to.
- I can't do that.

52:35.160 --> 52:38.089
Eat it. Come on. Take it. I gotta drive.
Ten and two on the wheels.

52:38.113 --> 52:40.391
Take it. Take it. Come on.

52:41.194 --> 52:42.762
There you go.

52:44.918 --> 52:48.438
- I can't do this Tony.
- Eat the goddamn thing.

52:49.204 --> 52:50.490
Jesus.

53:00.705 --> 53:02.140
What, no good?

53:08.011 --> 53:09.633
Just seems...

53:10.889 --> 53:12.996
so unsanitary.

53:13.052 --> 53:14.885
Who gives a shit?

53:14.989 --> 53:17.205
Just relax and enjoy it.

53:17.325 --> 53:19.580
My father used to say,

53:20.185 --> 53:22.768
whatever you do, do
it a hundred percent.

53:23.043 --> 53:25.712
When you work, work,
when you laugh, laugh,

53:25.957 --> 53:28.860
when you eat, eat like
it's your last meal.

53:29.314 --> 53:32.787
You want another piece?
Here, have a breast.

53:32.814 --> 53:34.280
Delicious.

53:35.302 --> 53:36.947
Take it. There you go.

53:37.255 --> 53:39.768
What do we do about the bones?

53:42.186 --> 53:43.675
We do this.

53:45.341 --> 53:47.276
This is what we do.

53:54.433 --> 53:56.141
There you go.

54:06.860 --> 54:10.474
What's the big deal with that?
Squirrels will eat it anyway.

54:48.148 --> 54:49.614
This can't be right.

54:52.000 --> 54:53.989
Says right here.

54:54.026 --> 54:56.671
Cozy as your own home.

54:57.462 --> 54:59.794
Place looks like my ass.

54:59.813 --> 55:01.544
This is the place.

55:07.466 --> 55:09.549
Square one please.

55:10.294 --> 55:13.048
- Just this one?
- Thank you.

55:16.299 --> 55:18.129
Hey... Uh...

55:18.153 --> 55:21.915
If you need anything, I'll be right
up the street at the Easton Inn.

55:22.393 --> 55:24.281
Thank you Tony.

55:28.509 --> 55:32.825
- Hey Floyd, we ready?
- Tulley, I can't play, my problem.

55:35.997 --> 55:39.525
Hey, fancy-pants, you wanna play?

55:40.014 --> 55:42.878
- I beg your pardon.
- Come on brother, we short in men.

55:44.238 --> 55:46.094
I... I'd rather not.

55:46.628 --> 55:48.953
What, you too high and mighty?

55:50.780 --> 55:53.906
He's just afraid of getting
that butler uniform all that dusty!

55:55.883 --> 55:57.825
I'm just...

55:58.425 --> 56:00.805
I'm on my way out
to meet a friend.

56:01.527 --> 56:03.305
Yeah, thanks for nothing?

56:06.002 --> 56:09.936
- Floyd, come on man.
- Shut your ass up man, leave me alone.

56:44.825 --> 56:47.814
Vacation without aggravation.

56:57.272 --> 57:00.628
Delightful dinners for particular people.

57:02.931 --> 57:05.654
- Yeah?
- Get up! It's George. Get up.

57:06.868 --> 57:09.545
Tony come on. Hurry up!

57:10.883 --> 57:12.625
Dr. Shirley's in trouble.

57:12.649 --> 57:14.555
I went out for a drink,
I walk into this bar,

57:14.579 --> 57:16.724
and Dr Shirley's in there
getting bounced around!

57:16.790 --> 57:19.211
I didn't want to leave him,
but I didn't know what to do!

57:19.235 --> 57:22.654
Who let him out of his cage? And
they put that little tie on him too?

57:22.720 --> 57:24.357
Who you are dressed out?

57:26.102 --> 57:27.912
Get your hands off him.

57:30.490 --> 57:33.568
What in the good goddamn
we got here, fellas?

57:33.592 --> 57:36.479
Hand him over, we walk
out, won't be a problem.

57:36.834 --> 57:39.188
I just wanted a drink Tony.

57:39.212 --> 57:41.998
Hey, I told you, we'll
leave. Not a big deal.

57:42.022 --> 57:42.834
Come on.

57:42.858 --> 57:46.156
He ain't going nowhere, we need a
Brillo pad to wash them dishes with.

57:46.180 --> 57:50.363
Listen assholes, do yourself
a favor and let him go.

57:50.687 --> 57:52.028
Now!

57:54.194 --> 57:55.941
Say it nice.

57:56.663 --> 57:58.511
I just said it nice.

57:58.967 --> 58:02.214
This boy's gonna get
what he's got coming to him.

58:04.118 --> 58:07.716
And you... you
ain't got no say!

58:10.488 --> 58:11.808
Maybe.

58:11.832 --> 58:14.210
But, whatever happens
here, I'm gonna put a

58:14.234 --> 58:17.079
bullet right in the middle
of your thick skull.

58:18.296 --> 58:20.410
He ain't got no gun, Ray.

58:20.445 --> 58:22.480
He's fulla shit.

58:22.757 --> 58:24.895
What if he ain't?

58:28.317 --> 58:30.329
Well, I sure ain't.

58:30.942 --> 58:34.431
And I ain't about to let this
come to pass in my place.

58:37.396 --> 58:40.330
Let the spook go. Let him go.

58:40.630 --> 58:41.979
Come on.

58:43.025 --> 58:45.006
Get him outta here.

58:45.342 --> 58:49.037
I want these Yankees
off from my property.

58:49.061 --> 58:51.839
- Go home.
- Come on George, go, go.

58:55.240 --> 58:56.581
Go home.

59:03.607 --> 59:04.731
You out of your mind?

59:04.755 --> 59:08.322
I'm sorry. I didn't mean
to put you in that position.

59:09.052 --> 59:10.621
Wait, wait, wait!

59:10.645 --> 59:13.079
You wanna throw up again?

59:14.922 --> 59:16.212
I'm OK.

59:16.236 --> 59:18.591
Hones to God Doc,
I don't understand you.

59:18.648 --> 59:21.452
You could have drunk here.
You got a whole bottle.

59:21.476 --> 59:23.924
- I just needed some air.
- Air?

59:23.948 --> 59:25.757
Do you know where you are?

59:26.940 --> 59:29.585
Does the geography
really matter?

59:30.272 --> 59:33.175
- What?
- If I was in a bar...

59:33.568 --> 59:35.977
in your neighborhood, would...

59:36.001 --> 59:38.857
the conversation be any different?

59:40.620 --> 59:43.516
From now on you don't go nowhere
without me.

59:43.735 --> 59:45.427
Nowhere!

59:46.040 --> 59:48.131
- Got it?
- I understand.

59:49.446 --> 59:52.115
- Where is your room?
- Tony.

59:52.999 --> 59:54.347
What?

59:55.435 --> 59:57.689
Do you really have a gun?

59:57.732 --> 59:59.572
'Course not.

01:00:00.194 --> 01:00:03.301
Doc, where's your goddamn room?

01:00:07.379 --> 01:00:09.688
- There it is.
- Come on. Over there?

01:00:09.933 --> 01:00:13.273
Let me get you to bed Doc. You got
a big show tomorrow night. C'mon.

01:00:35.429 --> 01:00:38.769
Louisville. Thank you for
your warm hospitality!

01:00:45.502 --> 01:00:47.460
Thank you.

01:00:54.714 --> 01:00:57.377
- Don't be lazy Tony, enunciate.
- I ain't.

01:00:57.401 --> 01:01:00.648
- Betty bought a bit of better butter.
- Betty bought.

01:01:01.104 --> 01:01:03.570
Betty bought... butter...

01:01:03.972 --> 01:01:05.627
Who says that?

01:01:05.651 --> 01:01:06.702
Butter uh...

01:01:06.726 --> 01:01:08.021
you have to start
somewhere Tony.

01:01:08.045 --> 01:01:11.553
A singer does vocal exercises, an
athlete warms up, before they rehearse.

01:01:11.577 --> 01:01:13.729
Athletes practice,
they don't rehearse.

01:01:15.248 --> 01:01:18.089
Ah, shit!

01:02:42.373 --> 01:02:47.784
Ladies and gentlemen, our very
special guest from the far north...

01:02:47.811 --> 01:02:49.480
Don Shirley!

01:02:53.053 --> 01:02:56.891
Accompanying Mr. Shirley,
the members of his trio...

01:02:56.915 --> 01:03:01.806
Oleg Malakhov, George
Dyer, and his associate,

01:03:01.830 --> 01:03:05.577
Tony Vallla... Valleg... Valle...
Valley... lohnja.

01:03:11.024 --> 01:03:13.729
This is my lovely wife Margaret.

01:03:13.753 --> 01:03:17.896
If you gentlemen don't mind, I'm going to
steal Donnie away for some introductions.

01:03:25.014 --> 01:03:27.417
- What's that?
- Pimiento-cheese sandwich, sir.

01:03:27.506 --> 01:03:29.378
Yeah, I'll try that one.

01:03:40.273 --> 01:03:42.294
Sorry! Not for me.

01:03:49.766 --> 01:03:54.323
Earlier this week, we asked our help
what Mr. Shirley might like for supper.

01:03:54.347 --> 01:03:58.289
So the boys in the kitchen whipped up
a special menu in honor of our guest.

01:03:58.367 --> 01:04:00.099
Gentlemen.

01:04:00.845 --> 01:04:03.232
Home cooked fried chicken.

01:04:09.719 --> 01:04:13.661
There you go. Bring them in.
Serve it up hot.

01:04:44.534 --> 01:04:46.995
Thank you.

01:04:47.019 --> 01:04:49.664
We return after a brief intermission.

01:04:52.401 --> 01:04:56.656
- Excuse me, Don. Lovely work in there.
- Why! Thank you!

01:04:57.000 --> 01:05:00.270
Are you looking for the commode?
Here, let me help you.

01:05:00.281 --> 01:05:02.809
Right out there 'fore that pine.

01:05:07.583 --> 01:05:09.439
I'd prefer not to use that.

01:05:09.856 --> 01:05:12.986
Well, don't be silly, Don. It
looks a lot worse from the outside.

01:05:13.106 --> 01:05:15.473
And I'd suppose you'd
know from experience.

01:05:15.497 --> 01:05:17.728
What? Never had any complains.

01:05:21.635 --> 01:05:25.405
Well, I could return to my motel
and use the facilities there.

01:05:26.330 --> 01:05:29.101
But... that would take
at least a half an hour.

01:05:32.501 --> 01:05:34.248
We don't mind waiting.

01:05:36.482 --> 01:05:39.495
Why don't I just pull over... You
can piss in the woods?

01:05:39.525 --> 01:05:41.181
Animals go in the woods.

01:05:41.205 --> 01:05:42.624
But it's gonna be at
least twenty minutes if

01:05:42.648 --> 01:05:44.108
I gotta go all the way
back to your motel.

01:05:44.132 --> 01:05:47.785
So let's just get there so I
can go back and finish the show.

01:05:48.276 --> 01:05:50.286
See, that's the difference
between you and me.

01:05:50.310 --> 01:05:52.979
- I'd have zero problem goin' in the woods.
- I'm well aware.

01:05:53.287 --> 01:05:56.489
Why you sore at me? I don't
make the rules down here.

01:05:56.513 --> 01:05:59.783
No? Then who does?

01:06:00.230 --> 01:06:03.464
Oh! you saying just 'cause
I'm white

01:06:03.488 --> 01:06:07.393
and they're white? You know, that's a very
prejudice thing you just said there.

01:06:07.417 --> 01:06:09.078
A very prejudice thing.

01:06:09.113 --> 01:06:11.824
I got more in common with the
hymies at Second Avenue Deli

01:06:11.848 --> 01:06:14.238
than I do with these
hillbilly pricks down here.

01:06:14.262 --> 01:06:16.530
- Eyes on the road.
- You always say that when

01:06:16.554 --> 01:06:19.461
- you don't like what I'm saying.
- Eyes on the road!

01:06:23.672 --> 01:06:25.352
I don't get it.

01:06:25.376 --> 01:06:28.419
How does he smile and shake
their hands like that?

01:06:28.786 --> 01:06:30.971
If they tried to pull
that outhouse shit on me,

01:06:30.995 --> 01:06:33.257
I'd piss right on their
living room floor.

01:06:34.683 --> 01:06:36.437
Don't do that.

01:06:38.058 --> 01:06:41.109
We have many concert dates left.

01:06:43.138 --> 01:06:45.184
Yeah... So...?

01:06:45.208 --> 01:06:48.799
You realize we are contractually
obliged to perform them?

01:06:49.427 --> 01:06:51.075
Of course I do.

01:06:51.099 --> 01:06:53.020
You don't play,
we don't get paid.

01:06:53.044 --> 01:06:54.799
What's your point?

01:06:55.021 --> 01:06:58.119
Ugly circumstances are
going to happen again.

01:06:58.125 --> 01:07:02.841
- So control yourself.
- Don't lecture me, you rat.

01:07:05.460 --> 01:07:07.753
Dr. Shirley could've
stayed up north getting

01:07:07.777 --> 01:07:09.739
rear-end kissed at
Park Avenue parties

01:07:09.763 --> 01:07:11.387
for three times money

01:07:11.645 --> 01:07:14.090
but he asked for this.

01:07:18.772 --> 01:07:20.355
Why?

01:07:39.314 --> 01:07:42.014
What on God's green
earth are you doing?

01:07:42.072 --> 01:07:43.612
A letter.

01:07:43.636 --> 01:07:46.139
Looks more like a
piecemeal ransom note.

01:07:46.917 --> 01:07:48.695
May I?

01:07:55.614 --> 01:07:58.094
Dear, Dolores...

01:07:58.118 --> 01:08:00.622
D-E-A-R, this isn't animal.

01:08:00.680 --> 01:08:05.177
I'm meeting all the highly
leading citizens of the town.

01:08:06.011 --> 01:08:09.539
People that use big words, all
of them

01:08:09.698 --> 01:08:12.142
but you know me, I get by,

01:08:12.166 --> 01:08:14.249
I'm a good bullshitter.

01:08:14.333 --> 01:08:16.479
Two “t”s in “bullshitter.”

01:08:16.817 --> 01:08:20.642
As I'm writing this letter,
I'm eating potato chips

01:08:20.825 --> 01:08:24.212
and I'm starting to get thirsty.

01:08:24.603 --> 01:08:28.178
I washed my socks and
dried them on the TV.

01:08:28.574 --> 01:08:32.634
- I should have brung the iron.
- You know this is pathetic right?

01:08:33.771 --> 01:08:36.206
Tell me what you're trying to say.

01:08:38.224 --> 01:08:41.533
- You know, how I miss her and shit.
- You didn't say that.

01:08:42.184 --> 01:08:45.463
But do it in a manner that no
one else has ever done it before.

01:08:45.567 --> 01:08:47.759
And without the profanity.

01:08:47.927 --> 01:08:52.439
Something like... Put this down.

01:08:54.316 --> 01:08:58.492
- Dear Dolores...
- Oh God no!

01:08:58.550 --> 01:09:01.547
D-E-A-R, Dolores.

01:09:03.366 --> 01:09:05.831
When-I-think-of-you...

01:09:06.551 --> 01:09:10.751
I'm-reminded of-the-beautiful
plains of Iowa.

01:09:11.024 --> 01:09:12.919
What planes?

01:09:13.155 --> 01:09:17.933
The plains. P-L-A-I-N-S.
Those big fields we saw.

01:09:18.615 --> 01:09:21.760
Yeah, those were nice.
PLAINS.

01:09:22.273 --> 01:09:29.448
Which what they call
big fields around here.

01:09:29.472 --> 01:09:31.354
Tony, no expounding.

01:09:31.378 --> 01:09:33.759
- A what?
- Just write what I say.

01:09:33.783 --> 01:09:37.944
- I'm good.
- The distance between us

01:09:39.011 --> 01:09:41.984
is breaking my spirit...

01:09:42.623 --> 01:09:44.551
between us...

01:09:44.575 --> 01:09:49.579
My time and experiences without
you are meaningless to me.

01:09:53.409 --> 01:09:57.046
Falling in love with you was the
easiest thing I have ever done.

01:09:57.410 --> 01:10:02.262
Falling... in love...
with you...

01:10:02.286 --> 01:10:05.313
is very fucking romantic.

01:10:05.337 --> 01:10:08.479
It was the easiest
thing I have ever done.

01:10:08.503 --> 01:10:11.420
Nothing matters to me but you.

01:10:11.553 --> 01:10:15.116
And everyday I am alive, I'm aware of this.

01:10:15.140 --> 01:10:19.116
I loved you the day I met
you, I love you today...

01:10:19.140 --> 01:10:22.723
And I will love you
to rest of my life.

01:10:25.064 --> 01:10:29.384
- So can I put the “P.S., kiss the kids”?
- A P.S.?

01:10:29.408 --> 01:10:31.584
Yeah, like a the end.

01:10:31.789 --> 01:10:36.091
That's like clanging a cowbell at
the end of Shostakovitch's 7th.

01:10:36.804 --> 01:10:40.114
Right... So that's good?

01:10:40.737 --> 01:10:42.672
It's perfect Tony.

01:10:46.531 --> 01:10:49.165
Everybody talks about
Willie Maze, 1954, wasn't

01:10:49.189 --> 01:10:51.689
even the greatest catcher
in the polo grounds.

01:10:51.713 --> 01:10:55.599
That was Joe, 1936,
2nd game at world

01:10:55.623 --> 01:10:58.991
series, final out, 500 feet...

01:11:02.388 --> 01:11:03.825
Do you like that Doc?

01:11:03.849 --> 01:11:06.846
- That's a handsome suit.
- Sharp.

01:11:07.269 --> 01:11:09.637
Guy looks just like you.

01:11:09.661 --> 01:11:11.758
He does?

01:11:12.714 --> 01:11:15.719
Oh... Size-wise. Yeah!

01:11:17.163 --> 01:11:19.629
He's about a forty two.

01:11:19.858 --> 01:11:22.089
Why don't you try on that?

01:11:22.920 --> 01:11:25.951
What, you gotta wear a
tuxedo on stage every night?

01:11:25.975 --> 01:11:28.123
You could mix it up a little back.

01:11:28.147 --> 01:11:31.152
Now, see how that looks on you.
We got plenty of time.

01:11:33.560 --> 01:11:35.713
I'll be right back.

01:11:35.771 --> 01:11:38.591
- How you doing?
- May I help you sir?

01:11:38.614 --> 01:11:41.692
Yeah. We wanna try on that
beautiful Grey suit in the window.

01:11:41.716 --> 01:11:44.393
- You got it in a 42?
- Of course.

01:11:46.990 --> 01:11:50.758
- That's the one.
- Dressing room's in the back, sir.

01:11:50.782 --> 01:11:53.476
Thank you. That'll
be just a moment.

01:11:53.500 --> 01:11:56.537
Take your time Doc, I'll
check out some ties for you.

01:11:57.574 --> 01:12:02.188
Uh, excuse me, you're not
allowed to try that on.

01:12:03.777 --> 01:12:05.309
I beg your pardon?

01:12:05.333 --> 01:12:10.143
If you would like to purchase it first,
we'll be happy to tailor it to your needs.

01:12:11.903 --> 01:12:13.629
I see.

01:13:16.111 --> 01:13:17.920
Yeah?

01:13:18.372 --> 01:13:20.173
F me.

01:13:32.934 --> 01:13:36.011
Hey officer, I got a
call about Dr. Shirley.

01:13:36.035 --> 01:13:37.596
Come on.

01:13:41.790 --> 01:13:44.420
His friends hate her.

01:13:44.717 --> 01:13:46.425
Thank you.

01:13:50.716 --> 01:13:53.725
Give the guy a towel,
for Chrissakes?

01:13:53.749 --> 01:13:55.420
- You the lawyer?
- No.

01:13:55.444 --> 01:13:57.598
Well you should call one.
We're taking your Auntie in.

01:13:57.622 --> 01:13:58.622
For what?

01:13:58.343 --> 01:14:01.043
Manager caught him
and the other guy...

01:14:04.690 --> 01:14:09.361
Can't we get the cuffs off him, let him
put his pants on? We talk about this?

01:14:09.385 --> 01:14:12.553
Sure we could. But we ain't.

01:14:12.603 --> 01:14:16.175
OK, look, we're out of
here tomorrow morning...

01:14:16.199 --> 01:14:20.404
you'll never see us again. There's gotta
be something due to work this out.

01:14:21.503 --> 01:14:25.187
What if, uh, you let him go, and I
give you something to thank you?

01:14:26.419 --> 01:14:30.461
- You bribing us?
- No. Hell no. A gift.

01:14:30.485 --> 01:14:34.302
- A thank you.
- What kind of thank you?

01:14:34.579 --> 01:14:39.833
Like... a donation to the police force.
To you guys.

01:14:39.954 --> 01:14:42.122
Whatever you want.

01:14:42.493 --> 01:14:44.633
You like suits?

01:14:44.657 --> 01:14:49.560
I was walking through your nice town today,
and I seen a store that was selling suits.

01:14:49.924 --> 01:14:51.707
Primo suits.

01:14:51.731 --> 01:14:57.306
What if... as a thank you... a
donation... I buy you each a suit?

01:14:58.438 --> 01:15:02.095
You get all dressed up, you take
the wife out for dinner.

01:15:02.119 --> 01:15:06.084
I mean... Guys like you, you
work hard, you deserve it.

01:15:13.226 --> 01:15:16.832
They were wrong for the way they
treated me, and you rewarded them.

01:15:18.424 --> 01:15:23.136
I was hired to get you from one show to the
next. How I do it shouldn't matter to you.

01:15:23.160 --> 01:15:26.500
- I just wish you hadn't paid them off.
- I did what I had to do.

01:15:27.338 --> 01:15:29.897
You know, if this got out
it would kill your career.

01:15:29.921 --> 01:15:31.452
OK. Tony.

01:15:31.557 --> 01:15:35.749
I need you to stop it with your phony
altruism and concern for my career.

01:15:36.013 --> 01:15:37.197
What the hell does that mean?

01:15:37.221 --> 01:15:39.360
You were only thinking
about yourself back there

01:15:39.384 --> 01:15:42.056
because you know if I miss a show,
it comes out of your pocket book.

01:15:42.080 --> 01:15:45.034
Of course I don't want you to miss
a show, you ungrateful bastard!

01:15:45.058 --> 01:15:47.123
You think I'm doing
this for my health?

01:15:47.147 --> 01:15:51.777
Tonight I saved your ass, so show
a little appreciation... Maybe?

01:15:51.801 --> 01:15:55.103
Besides, I told you never
to go nowhere without me!

01:15:56.088 --> 01:15:59.570
I assumed you would want
this to be the exception.

01:16:34.706 --> 01:16:38.463
Want me to get some makeup or
something before the show?

01:16:38.487 --> 01:16:39.848
No I'm fine.

01:16:39.872 --> 01:16:43.713
- You sure? Bruise kindda shrugs.
- I said I'm fine.

01:16:44.911 --> 01:16:46.541
Okay.

01:17:00.061 --> 01:17:02.082
Tony Lip?

01:17:02.113 --> 01:17:04.831
Dominic. The hell you
guys doing here?

01:17:04.855 --> 01:17:08.188
Brooklyn sent us down...
take care of a few things.

01:17:42.350 --> 01:17:44.909
I am working here.

01:17:52.842 --> 01:17:55.698
Sorry Doc, they are some
friends from New York.

01:17:56.404 --> 01:17:59.604
Hey, you get Dr Shirley's luggage?
Alright.

01:18:32.329 --> 01:18:35.154
Called his room. He'll be
down in a minute.

01:18:44.331 --> 01:18:47.149
- Hey Doc.
- Where are you off to?

01:18:48.875 --> 01:18:52.934
Just going downstairs.
To have a drink.

01:19:03.354 --> 01:19:05.252
Tony...

01:19:05.276 --> 01:19:08.375
I think you're doing
a wonderful job.

01:19:08.456 --> 01:19:10.414
So...

01:19:11.048 --> 01:19:14.797
I would like to formally offer you
the position of my road manager.

01:19:14.821 --> 01:19:16.545
With the title...

01:19:16.569 --> 01:19:19.378
also comes more responsibility but

01:19:19.764 --> 01:19:22.238
that also means a raise in pay.

01:19:22.303 --> 01:19:25.847
No. No. No, thanks.

01:19:27.443 --> 01:19:31.872
I mean, we agreed on a hundred and
twenty-five a week, plus expenses.

01:19:31.896 --> 01:19:34.564
That's our deal. Right?

01:19:36.074 --> 01:19:40.431
I ain't goin' nowhere, Doc. I was
just goin' down to tell 'em.

01:19:50.681 --> 01:19:52.577
Tony...

01:19:56.778 --> 01:19:59.337
I'm sorry about last night.

01:20:02.702 --> 01:20:05.089
Don't worry about it.

01:20:06.483 --> 01:20:09.750
I been working nightclubs in
the New York city my whole life...

01:20:09.774 --> 01:20:11.581
I know it's...

01:20:12.298 --> 01:20:14.295
complicated world.

01:20:26.665 --> 01:20:29.349
So, where'd you learn
how to play like that?

01:20:29.373 --> 01:20:30.547
My mother.

01:20:30.571 --> 01:20:33.037
Your mother... Really?

01:20:34.585 --> 01:20:37.785
She taught me how to
play in an old spinet.

01:20:38.359 --> 01:20:40.761
Soon as I could walk.

01:20:40.785 --> 01:20:43.672
Travel around the Florida panhandle...

01:20:43.699 --> 01:20:47.031
Put on my little shows
and perishes in halls...

01:20:47.091 --> 01:20:49.154
Fortunately a man who
had seen me play

01:20:49.178 --> 01:20:52.815
arranged for me to study at the
Leningrad Conservatory of Music.

01:20:53.027 --> 01:20:55.508
I was the first Negro
ever accepted there.

01:20:55.571 --> 01:20:58.323
So that's where they taught
you all them songs you play?

01:20:58.347 --> 01:21:00.906
Actually, I was trained
to play classical music.

01:21:00.930 --> 01:21:05.974
Brahms, Franz Liszt,
Beethoven, Chopin...

01:21:06.595 --> 01:21:09.451
it's all I ever wanted to play.

01:21:09.537 --> 01:21:15.049
But I was persuaded by my record company to
pursue a career in popular music instead.

01:21:15.546 --> 01:21:17.862
They insisted that
audiences would never

01:21:17.886 --> 01:21:20.738
accept a negro pianist
on the classical stage.

01:21:20.955 --> 01:21:24.515
Wanted to turn me into just
another “colored entertainer.”

01:21:25.330 --> 01:21:27.253
You know the guy who...

01:21:27.277 --> 01:21:32.636
smoking while he's playing, sets a glass of
whiskey on his piano and then he complains

01:21:32.660 --> 01:21:35.900
because he's not respected
like Arthur Rubinstein.

01:21:36.100 --> 01:21:41.643
You don't see Arthur Rubenstein putting
a glass of whiskey on his piano.

01:21:42.702 --> 01:21:44.000
I don't know...

01:21:44.024 --> 01:21:48.075
I think if you stuck to that classic
stuff it would've been a big mistake.

01:21:48.099 --> 01:21:52.752
A mistake? Performing the music I
trained my entire life to play?

01:21:52.787 --> 01:21:55.402
Trained? What are you, a seal?

01:21:55.426 --> 01:21:57.046
People love what you do.

01:21:57.070 --> 01:22:02.279
Anyone can sound like Beethoven or
Joe Pan or them other guys you said.

01:22:02.303 --> 01:22:06.854
But your music, what you do...

01:22:07.486 --> 01:22:10.225
Only you can do that.

01:22:12.325 --> 01:22:14.252
Thank you Tony.

01:22:18.210 --> 01:22:21.121
But... not everyone can play
Chopin...

01:22:22.406 --> 01:22:24.418
not like I can.

01:22:28.604 --> 01:22:31.135
The trees have shed
their leafy clothing

01:22:31.159 --> 01:22:34.216
and their colors have faded
to grays and browns.

01:22:34.240 --> 01:22:40.210
I saw a millions of trees all dusted
with snow just like out of a fairy tale.

01:22:40.234 --> 01:22:42.455
Oh, he's so expressive.

01:22:42.727 --> 01:22:45.327
Gotta admit, Lip's letters...

01:22:45.351 --> 01:22:48.131
- They are not bad.
- Oh well! It's in the family.

01:22:48.155 --> 01:22:50.801
They say our great,
great, great grandfather

01:22:50.825 --> 01:22:53.210
helped Da Vinci with
the Sixteen Chapel.

01:22:53.234 --> 01:22:54.704
You mean Michelangelo?

01:22:54.728 --> 01:22:55.704
Right.

01:22:55.728 --> 01:22:58.024
What is Michelangelo have
to do with writing letters?

01:22:58.048 --> 01:23:02.568
- I'm just saying, we're an arty family.
- I would count the hours...

01:23:02.592 --> 01:23:07.310
minutes... and seconds...
until you are in my arms.

01:23:07.334 --> 01:23:09.148
Love you, Tony.

01:23:09.172 --> 01:23:11.451
P.S. KISS THE KIDS.

01:23:11.738 --> 01:23:14.239
- John.
- Yeah?

01:23:14.263 --> 01:23:16.075
I want a letter.

01:23:16.099 --> 01:23:18.438
Yeah, as soon as you make a meal.

01:23:32.914 --> 01:23:35.958
Eyes on the road.

01:24:00.418 --> 01:24:01.667
Tony.

01:24:01.691 --> 01:24:05.639
Alright everybody! Let's
give a finest Louisiana

01:24:05.663 --> 01:24:09.809
welcome to Don Shirley and
the Don Shirley Trio!

01:24:35.297 --> 01:24:39.793
Your mother's ass... piece of shit.

01:24:47.429 --> 01:24:49.808
Hell's this guy doing?

01:24:52.431 --> 01:24:55.068
Son of a bitch.

01:25:06.931 --> 01:25:09.459
License and papers?

01:25:09.786 --> 01:25:11.926
Am I glad to see you.

01:25:11.950 --> 01:25:16.838
We had a turn off from main road...
and uh, now we're lost.

01:25:18.379 --> 01:25:21.569
- Step out of the car.
- What I do?

01:25:21.593 --> 01:25:23.754
Out of the car.

01:25:34.884 --> 01:25:37.235
Why you on this road?

01:25:37.259 --> 01:25:41.982
I told you, we had to make
a detour and we got lost.

01:25:45.928 --> 01:25:48.523
And why you driving him?

01:25:48.547 --> 01:25:50.722
He's my boss.

01:25:56.181 --> 01:26:00.542
He can't be out here at night.
This is a sundown town.

01:26:00.566 --> 01:26:02.288
What's that?

01:26:03.183 --> 01:26:09.438
- Get him out of the car. Check his I.D.
- Come on, it's pouring rain sir.

01:26:09.462 --> 01:26:11.874
I can just get it right
here through the window.

01:26:11.898 --> 01:26:13.243
Get him out of the car!

01:26:13.267 --> 01:26:16.139
- Come on.
- Get out now! Get out!

01:26:16.720 --> 01:26:18.889
You got ID?

01:26:20.857 --> 01:26:23.481
How you say this last name?

01:26:23.505 --> 01:26:25.815
Vallelonga.

01:26:26.068 --> 01:26:28.277
'Hell kind of name is that?

01:26:28.301 --> 01:26:29.975
It's Italian.

01:26:29.999 --> 01:26:35.230
Oh, now I see. That's why you
driving him around.

01:26:36.767 --> 01:26:38.990
You half a nigger yourself.

01:26:40.205 --> 01:26:44.030
Hands in the air, now, now!

01:26:46.579 --> 01:26:48.279
Excuse me.

01:26:51.921 --> 01:26:53.879
Excuse me, sirs.

01:26:56.171 --> 01:26:58.705
I understand why my
associate is being held,

01:26:58.729 --> 01:27:01.293
but what exactly am I
being charged with?

01:27:04.738 --> 01:27:07.236
You seem like reasonable men.

01:27:07.566 --> 01:27:11.151
Perhaps you could let me out so that we
could discuss the situation further?

01:27:11.175 --> 01:27:16.015
Just put the apple butter away, boy.
You ain't goin' nowhere no time soon.

01:27:16.833 --> 01:27:20.939
- You cannot hold me without cause!
- Well I got cause.

01:27:20.974 --> 01:27:24.339
'Cause you let the sun
set on your black ass!

01:27:25.325 --> 01:27:29.884
I want to speak to my
lawyer, I want my call!

01:27:29.908 --> 01:27:33.038
This is a flagrant
violation of my rights!

01:27:33.310 --> 01:27:35.081
You know...

01:27:36.373 --> 01:27:41.096
He does have... rights.

01:27:45.428 --> 01:27:49.941
Give the negro his goddamn phone call.
You happy?

01:27:54.358 --> 01:27:58.160
You know a lawyer? Call him.

01:28:15.095 --> 01:28:18.787
As my mother always said, “What
kind of brand new fool are you?!”

01:28:19.337 --> 01:28:21.202
Look at them over there.

01:28:21.226 --> 01:28:24.744
Take a good look at the officer you hit.
Look at him.

01:28:24.768 --> 01:28:28.578
He's over there having a grand
old time, chatting up his pals

01:28:28.667 --> 01:28:32.188
enjoying a nice cup of coffee.
And where are you?

01:28:32.212 --> 01:28:35.990
In here, with me,
who did nothing.

01:28:36.167 --> 01:28:38.019
Yet I'm the one who's
pays the price.

01:28:38.043 --> 01:28:40.699
I'm the one who's gonna
miss the Birmingham show.

01:28:40.723 --> 01:28:44.081
Hey, I'm losing a lot of money,
too, if you don't play Birmingham.

01:28:44.105 --> 01:28:47.962
So that little temper
tantrum... was it worth it?

01:28:50.869 --> 01:28:54.485
You don't win with violence,
Tony, you win when you

01:28:54.509 --> 01:28:58.045
maintain your dignity.
Dignity always prevails.

01:28:58.653 --> 01:29:02.509
And tonight, because
of you, we did not.

01:29:07.380 --> 01:29:10.182
I wouldn't touch that mattress Doc.

01:29:14.735 --> 01:29:16.248
No sir.

01:29:16.470 --> 01:29:19.428
No. No I'm not sir.

01:29:19.541 --> 01:29:22.217
Yes, sir, he's right
here, yes sir.

01:29:22.564 --> 01:29:25.163
- Yes sir.
- Give me.

01:29:25.260 --> 01:29:28.788
Chief Pratt... who's this?
Bull-oney.

01:29:31.240 --> 01:29:32.748
Yes sir.

01:29:32.772 --> 01:29:35.238
I can hear it now, Governor.

01:29:39.475 --> 01:29:42.738
No sir, I'm sorry. But, of course
I recognize your voice.

01:29:45.906 --> 01:29:47.785
Sir...

01:29:48.354 --> 01:29:52.336
You saying the boy we got
locked up called who?

01:29:54.858 --> 01:29:57.776
Oh, and he called you?

01:29:58.056 --> 01:30:01.538
No sir, but an officer was
assaulted in the line of...

01:30:04.940 --> 01:30:09.436
No, no, I don't want no National Guard
coming down here, neither, sir.

01:30:10.543 --> 01:30:13.040
Yes, Governor, immediately.

01:30:13.301 --> 01:30:16.126
Good night to you
and the missus.

01:30:19.743 --> 01:30:21.826
- Get them out.
- What?!

01:30:22.006 --> 01:30:25.401
- Cut 'em goddamn loose.
- That dago-wop hit me!

01:30:25.436 --> 01:30:28.134
You keep your goddamn job?
Then you do what I goddamn

01:30:28.158 --> 01:30:31.381
tell you to do, when I
goddamn tell you to do it.

01:30:31.405 --> 01:30:33.941
Now I'm telling you to
get 'em the goddamn out.

01:30:34.139 --> 01:30:36.949
Who the hell did you call?

01:30:38.593 --> 01:30:44.183
Bobby Kennedy just saved our asses!
Maddon... How great is that?!

01:30:44.183 --> 01:30:45.964
It's not great.

01:30:45.988 --> 01:30:48.364
It's not great at
Al, it's humiliating.

01:30:48.388 --> 01:30:52.298
'The hell you talking about?
We were screwed, now we ain't.

01:30:52.491 --> 01:30:55.130
And I just put the Attorney
General of the United

01:30:55.154 --> 01:30:57.886
- States in an incredibly awkward position.
- So what?

01:30:57.910 --> 01:31:00.821
That's what the guy gets paid for.
What else he got to do?

01:31:00.909 --> 01:31:04.743
That man and his brother are
trying to change this country,

01:31:04.767 --> 01:31:06.688
that's what else he's got to do!

01:31:07.744 --> 01:31:10.054
Now he thinks I'm
some kind of...

01:31:11.401 --> 01:31:16.206
Calling from some backwoods swamp jail,
asking to attenuate assault charges...

01:31:16.230 --> 01:31:17.516
who does that?

01:31:17.661 --> 01:31:20.002
Garbage, that's who.

01:31:20.415 --> 01:31:21.539
You shouldn't have hit him.

01:31:21.563 --> 01:31:25.018
I didn't like the way he was treating you,
making you stand out in the rain like that.

01:31:25.042 --> 01:31:28.367
Please, you hit him because
of what he called you.

01:31:28.514 --> 01:31:30.719
I've had to endure that kind
of talk my entire life,

01:31:30.743 --> 01:31:32.468
you should be able to take
it for at least one night.

01:31:32.492 --> 01:31:35.570
What, I can't get mad at that stuff
he was saying 'cause I ain't black?

01:31:35.594 --> 01:31:38.092
- Christ, I'm blacker than you.
- Excuse me?

01:31:38.116 --> 01:31:40.621
You don't know shit
about your own people!

01:31:40.645 --> 01:31:43.295
What they eat, how they
talk, how they live.

01:31:43.319 --> 01:31:45.060
You don't even know
who Lil' Richard is!

01:31:45.084 --> 01:31:48.489
Oh so knowing who Little Richard
is makes you blacker than me?

01:31:48.786 --> 01:31:51.268
Oh Tony, I wish you could
hear yourself sometimes

01:31:51.292 --> 01:31:53.851
- you wouldn't talk so damn much.
- Bullshit.

01:31:53.933 --> 01:31:56.350
I know exactly who I am.

01:31:56.374 --> 01:31:59.670
I'm the guy who's lived on the same
neighborhood in the Bronx my entire life,

01:31:59.694 --> 01:32:02.302
with my mother, my father, my
brother, and now my wife and kids.

01:32:02.326 --> 01:32:04.538
That's it, that's who I am.

01:32:04.562 --> 01:32:08.106
I'm the asshole who's gotta hustle every
goddamn day to put food out on table.

01:32:08.130 --> 01:32:11.895
You? Mr. Big Shot? You
live on top of a castle

01:32:11.919 --> 01:32:14.537
traveling around the world doing
concerts for rich people...

01:32:14.561 --> 01:32:17.346
I live on the streets,
you sit on a throne

01:32:17.370 --> 01:32:20.601
so yeah, my world is way
more blacker than yours!

01:32:21.257 --> 01:32:23.230
Pull over.

01:32:23.320 --> 01:32:25.421
- What?
- Pull over.

01:32:25.445 --> 01:32:28.614
- I ain't pulling over!
- Stop the car Tony!

01:32:30.406 --> 01:32:31.965
What?

01:32:32.093 --> 01:32:34.449
What are you doing?!

01:32:37.757 --> 01:32:40.043
Doc, what the hell are you doing?

01:32:40.109 --> 01:32:42.874
Doc, get back in the car.

01:32:42.898 --> 01:32:46.363
Yes, I live in a castle!
Tony. Alone!

01:32:47.083 --> 01:32:49.307
And rich white people pay
me to play piano for

01:32:49.331 --> 01:32:51.565
them, because it makes
them feel cultured.

01:32:51.667 --> 01:32:53.361
But as soon as I
step off that stage

01:32:53.385 --> 01:32:56.055
I go right back to being
just another nigger to them.

01:32:56.518 --> 01:32:59.277
Because that is
their true culture.

01:32:59.301 --> 01:33:02.721
And I suffer that slight alone, because
I'm not accepted by my own people,

01:33:02.745 --> 01:33:04.796
because I'm not
like them either!

01:33:05.420 --> 01:33:08.283
So if I'm not black enough,
and if I'm not white enough,

01:33:08.307 --> 01:33:11.912
and if I'm not man enough,
then tell me Tony, what am I?!

01:33:45.771 --> 01:33:48.339
I need some sleep.

01:33:51.270 --> 01:33:52.595
A'right.

01:33:53.379 --> 01:33:56.790
I'll stop by the next place we see
and I'll sneak you into my room.

01:33:56.814 --> 01:34:01.598
No. No. I refuse to stay in an
establishment where I'm not welcome.

01:34:04.385 --> 01:34:07.179
Yeah. OK.

01:34:24.057 --> 01:34:26.960
Tony, do you have to smoke everywhere?

01:34:28.596 --> 01:34:30.858
I didn't know it would bother you.

01:34:30.885 --> 01:34:33.023
Should have told me.

01:34:33.430 --> 01:34:36.512
All you gotta do, is say the word Doc.

01:34:48.696 --> 01:34:52.130
You do realize you'd be home
before that letter arrives?

01:34:52.383 --> 01:34:53.958
Yeah, I know.

01:34:53.981 --> 01:34:57.603
Just thought of bringing it with me.
Save on the stamps.

01:34:57.709 --> 01:35:01.995
A'right, Tony. Give
it here, I'll fix it.

01:35:02.637 --> 01:35:07.282
No offense, Doc, but I think
I got the hang of it now.

01:35:14.108 --> 01:35:18.699
Dear Dolores. Sometimes
you remind me of a house.

01:35:21.696 --> 01:35:24.867
A house with beautiful
lights on it

01:35:24.891 --> 01:35:27.739
where everyone happy inside.

01:35:32.466 --> 01:35:36.346
Yes, Tony! You go it.

01:35:39.249 --> 01:35:41.160
Thanks.

01:35:43.688 --> 01:35:48.435
Doc, thanks for helping
me with the letters.

01:35:48.570 --> 01:35:53.168
- You're really good at writing them.
- My pleasure Tony.

01:35:54.413 --> 01:35:59.964
You know, when you get home, maybe you
should write one to your brother?

01:36:02.105 --> 01:36:05.352
He knows where I am if he
ever wants to reconnect.

01:36:05.683 --> 01:36:09.039
If... I wouldn't wait.

01:36:09.316 --> 01:36:15.336
You know... the world's full of lonely
people afraid to make the first move.

01:36:36.332 --> 01:36:40.384
You know Doc, something's been
eating at me this whole trip.

01:36:43.946 --> 01:36:46.689
That Tittsburgh was a
major disappointment.

01:36:46.713 --> 01:36:49.752
I didn't notice any difference at all.
Did you?

01:36:49.776 --> 01:36:51.804
Good night Tony.

01:37:04.106 --> 01:37:06.705
- Good Evening. Welcome.
- Welcome. Come on in.

01:37:14.097 --> 01:37:16.179
Welcome Mr Shirley.

01:37:16.229 --> 01:37:19.909
Graham Kindell, I'm the general manager.
It is a pleasure to meet you.

01:37:19.933 --> 01:37:23.066
Thank you, Mr. Kindell. This
is Mr. Tony Vallelonga.

01:37:23.090 --> 01:37:24.801
- Nice to meet you, Tony.
- How you doing?

01:37:24.825 --> 01:37:29.429
Let's keep the car right here on our guest
of honor spot. Right this way, gentlemen.

01:37:29.453 --> 01:37:31.761
- How was your drive up?
- Oh it's wonderful.

01:37:31.785 --> 01:37:33.305
Good to hear, good to hear.

01:37:33.329 --> 01:37:36.020
As you can imagine our Christmas
show is the biggest show of

01:37:36.044 --> 01:37:38.962
the year and we are so happy
to have you here Mr Shirley.

01:37:38.986 --> 01:37:42.243
So, if you need anything... anything
t'all... you let me know.

01:37:42.267 --> 01:37:44.650
- Oh thank you.
- Now, here we are...

01:37:44.674 --> 01:37:47.682
I got about an hour before show time.
Any questions?

01:37:48.237 --> 01:37:49.820
Where's the restaurant?

01:37:49.844 --> 01:37:53.641
Well, you continue down the hall here,
Tony, to the right, across the lobby.

01:37:53.665 --> 01:37:57.107
- Good luck! Break a leg.
- Thank you.

01:37:58.058 --> 01:38:01.652
He said we've got an hour.
You must be starving Doc.

01:38:01.676 --> 01:38:03.695
Go ahead, I'll meet you there.

01:38:29.480 --> 01:38:31.422
May we join you?

01:38:32.782 --> 01:38:34.263
Get in.

01:38:39.372 --> 01:38:42.150
- Cocktail, gentlemen?
- I'm good.

01:38:42.275 --> 01:38:45.421
- 3 shots Vodka.
- Whoa!

01:38:45.624 --> 01:38:49.589
Last show. Cold war over.
Time for truce.

01:38:50.674 --> 01:38:53.714
- Is Dr Shirley in his dressing room?
- Yeah.

01:38:53.738 --> 01:38:55.534
More like a broom closet.

01:38:55.558 --> 01:38:58.696
Tell you, I don't know why he
puts up with that shit.

01:39:02.321 --> 01:39:06.013
Six years ago, in 1956,

01:39:06.150 --> 01:39:11.975
Nat King Cole was invited to perform at the
Municipal Auditorium here in Birmingham.

01:39:12.680 --> 01:39:17.712
Mr. Cole was the first negro asked to play
at a white establishment in this city.

01:39:17.736 --> 01:39:21.062
As soon as he started playing,
a group of men attacked him

01:39:21.086 --> 01:39:23.202
for playing white
people's music.

01:39:23.905 --> 01:39:26.284
They pulled him off stage

01:39:26.795 --> 01:39:29.050
beat him badly.

01:39:29.051 --> 01:39:31.665
Jesus Christ!

01:39:34.318 --> 01:39:36.737
You asked once

01:39:36.772 --> 01:39:39.417
why Dr. Shirley does this?

01:39:40.064 --> 01:39:41.716
I tell you.

01:39:41.740 --> 01:39:47.744
Because genius is not enough. It takes
courage to change people's hearts.

01:39:55.633 --> 01:39:57.364
Thanks.

01:39:57.797 --> 01:39:59.434
Thank you.

01:40:27.205 --> 01:40:30.150
- I understand but...
- What's going on?

01:40:30.174 --> 01:40:34.485
This gentleman says that I'm
not permitted dine here.

01:40:34.509 --> 01:40:37.666
No, you don't understand, he's
playing tonight, he's the main event.

01:40:37.690 --> 01:40:41.298
I'm sorry. But it's the
policy of the restaurant.

01:40:41.322 --> 01:40:44.166
- Everything all right?
- No, it's not all right.

01:40:44.190 --> 01:40:46.925
This guy is saying Dr
Shirley can't eat here.

01:40:46.949 --> 01:40:51.088
Well, I apologize, but these are...
longstanding traditions.

01:40:51.112 --> 01:40:53.622
Club rules. I'm sure
you understand.

01:40:53.646 --> 01:40:56.101
No. I do not understand.

01:41:01.399 --> 01:41:02.927
I'm sorry.

01:41:02.968 --> 01:41:05.575
Wait a minute, are you
tellin' me the bozos

01:41:05.599 --> 01:41:08.242
in his band, and these
people that came here

01:41:08.266 --> 01:41:13.441
to see him play, they can eat here, but the
star of the show, spot of honor, he can't.

01:41:13.904 --> 01:41:15.320
I'm afraid not.

01:41:15.344 --> 01:41:19.167
Well he's gotta eat, I mean
he's gotta have dinner.

01:41:20.618 --> 01:41:23.291
I tell you what. Why don't
we bring something to

01:41:23.315 --> 01:41:25.956
his dressing room, huh?
John, show him the menu.

01:41:25.980 --> 01:41:30.375
No. I'm not eating in
that storage room.

01:41:31.105 --> 01:41:34.979
Okay... if you'd prefer, there's a
very popular establishment right

01:41:35.003 --> 01:41:38.790
down the road, the Orange Bird,
they'd be happy to feed you.

01:41:40.992 --> 01:41:42.840
Doc, come here.

01:41:44.335 --> 01:41:45.739
One second just.

01:41:46.406 --> 01:41:50.600
C'mon, maybe that place is better anyway.
The dinner rolls here are like rocks.

01:41:50.624 --> 01:41:53.465
Let's just go over...
just go and come back.

01:41:57.597 --> 01:41:59.922
It's the last show.

01:41:59.977 --> 01:42:02.443
Bottom of the knife. Let's
just get it over with

01:42:02.467 --> 01:42:05.232
and we can go home and get
away from these pricks.

01:42:06.938 --> 01:42:10.920
Ah, there you go, the fish
is wonderful tonight.

01:42:16.094 --> 01:42:21.442
Either I eat in this room,
or I'm not performing tonight.

01:42:24.950 --> 01:42:28.150
May I have a word with you?

01:42:41.267 --> 01:42:45.474
Mr. Villanueva, you have to talk sense to
Mr. Shirley. Please make him understand

01:42:45.498 --> 01:42:49.810
we're not insulting him personally, this
is just the way things are done down here.

01:42:49.834 --> 01:42:51.942
Yeah, well he's not
from down here.

01:42:51.966 --> 01:42:54.350
Just ask him to be reasonable.
I got 400 guests

01:42:54.374 --> 01:42:56.757
in there who expect to
be entertained tonight.

01:42:56.781 --> 01:42:58.930
And Dr. Shirley expects
to eat tonight.

01:42:58.954 --> 01:43:01.863
Why can't you just make an
exception this one time?

01:43:03.157 --> 01:43:05.492
Lemme tell you a story.

01:43:05.516 --> 01:43:09.450
You ever hear of the Boston
Celtics basketball club?

01:43:09.489 --> 01:43:13.658
Yeah, those boys came through here a
couple years ago on a barnstorming tour.

01:43:13.682 --> 01:43:15.355
Now, seeing as they were World
Champions of the league and all, we

01:43:15.379 --> 01:43:19.648
were tickled to have 'em eat here,
we rolled out the welcome wagon.

01:43:19.918 --> 01:43:23.275
So do you know what table their
big coon ate at that night?

01:43:24.367 --> 01:43:26.813
- No.
- I don't either.

01:43:26.837 --> 01:43:30.583
But it wasn't one of ours.
Now let's cut the bullshit.

01:43:30.607 --> 01:43:32.491
Tell me what it's gonna take.

01:43:32.515 --> 01:43:36.221
Say one hundred dollars and
you get your boy to play?

01:43:37.450 --> 01:43:39.829
You think you can buy me?

01:43:39.831 --> 01:43:42.047
With all due respect,
sir, but you wouldn't be

01:43:42.071 --> 01:43:45.090
in a job like this if
you couldn't be bought.

01:43:45.164 --> 01:43:47.481
Stop! Tony.

01:43:48.766 --> 01:43:50.973
It's alright.

01:43:52.606 --> 01:43:54.782
I'll play.

01:43:55.012 --> 01:43:57.169
If you want me to.

01:44:12.195 --> 01:44:14.575
Let's get the fuck outta here.

01:44:14.625 --> 01:44:17.242
What do you mean,
let's get outta here?

01:44:17.266 --> 01:44:19.687
Where the hell do you
think you're going?

01:44:19.711 --> 01:44:21.727
Don, don't do this! Now you
signed a contract.

01:44:21.751 --> 01:44:24.505
And I know you're the kind of
man who honors a contract!

01:44:26.111 --> 01:44:29.009
You got a show to do, mister!
You turn yourself

01:44:29.033 --> 01:44:31.647
around. Right now goddammit!
Right now!

01:44:32.127 --> 01:44:35.847
This is why you people don't work
down here, cause you're unreliable.

01:44:35.871 --> 01:44:39.844
You hear me? I shipped that goddamn
Steinway in from Atlanta for you.

01:44:46.574 --> 01:44:48.110
Tony.

01:44:48.246 --> 01:44:49.816
Are you hungry?

01:44:49.840 --> 01:44:51.891
Does Betty like butter?

01:45:36.942 --> 01:45:41.001
- You a cop?
- Do I look Irish?

01:45:41.025 --> 01:45:45.006
- What you want, baby?
- Two Cutty's, neat.

01:45:53.518 --> 01:45:56.363
Whatever your specialty
is, we'll take it.

01:45:56.387 --> 01:45:59.080
Two orange birds!

01:46:10.779 --> 01:46:13.177
I like what you did
back there, Doc.

01:46:13.201 --> 01:46:15.596
You stood up for yourself.

01:46:17.281 --> 01:46:21.528
It's like your friend the
President says “Ask not

01:46:22.546 --> 01:46:25.050
your country what you could do for it,

01:46:25.264 --> 01:46:27.949
ask what you do for yourself.”

01:46:32.586 --> 01:46:34.351
So, darlin',

01:46:34.375 --> 01:46:37.189
what you do, all
dressed up like that?

01:46:37.213 --> 01:46:39.694
Nothing particularly important.

01:46:40.318 --> 01:46:43.245
Shouldn't judge a man by his clothes.

01:46:43.591 --> 01:46:46.707
He's only the greatest piano player
in the world.

01:46:46.731 --> 01:46:49.713
That right? You good?

01:46:50.713 --> 01:46:56.906
- Don't be shy, Doc. Tell her who you are.
- Don't tell me nothing, show me.

01:47:03.027 --> 01:47:05.001
Man...

01:50:23.562 --> 01:50:25.433
That's how you break a peak.

01:50:27.702 --> 01:50:31.598
Oh, that was a good time, I do
that once a month for free.

01:50:31.788 --> 01:50:34.363
- You're unbelievable.
- Hey Tony.

01:50:35.109 --> 01:50:37.477
I bet if we leave right
now, we can make it.

01:50:37.501 --> 01:50:41.598
- Make what?
- Christmas Eve. In New York city.

01:50:57.111 --> 01:51:00.686
Don't ever flash a wad
of cash in a bar.

01:51:10.022 --> 01:51:12.144
I knew you had a gun!

01:51:36.674 --> 01:51:38.881
It's getting bad Doc.

01:51:39.525 --> 01:51:41.186
Yes.

01:51:41.569 --> 01:51:44.909
It's a shame we don't have something
to protect us on our journey.

01:51:45.238 --> 01:51:50.219
Oh I know, why don't you put your
lucky rock up on the dash, Tony?

01:51:51.950 --> 01:51:56.470
C'mon Tony, we need all
the help we can get.

01:52:00.909 --> 01:52:04.265
Thank you. I feel safer already.

01:52:06.260 --> 01:52:08.960
You're a prick, you know that?

01:52:32.020 --> 01:52:34.524
Ah, shit!

01:52:43.354 --> 01:52:46.280
Goddamn cops.

01:52:56.211 --> 01:53:00.591
- What are you doing out here?
- We're trying to get to New York.

01:53:02.260 --> 01:53:05.780
- Is there a problem, Officer?
- Yeah.

01:53:05.818 --> 01:53:10.782
I noticed your car was tilting to the left.
Looks like your back tire's flat.

01:53:16.022 --> 01:53:17.518
Ah!

01:53:25.481 --> 01:53:28.353
Keep it moving, keep it moving.

01:53:41.440 --> 01:53:43.554
OK. Be careful gentlemen.

01:53:43.557 --> 01:53:48.521
- Merry Christmas!
- Merry Christmas! Thanks officer.

01:53:59.699 --> 01:54:02.822
Weather advisory warning
this Christmas Eve, as a

01:54:02.846 --> 01:54:05.820
major snowstorm is hitting
the eastern seaboard

01:54:05.844 --> 01:54:09.029
with the severest weather
in eastern Pennsylvania,

01:54:09.053 --> 01:54:11.812
northern New Jersey and
the five boroughs.

01:54:11.836 --> 01:54:15.430
Travelers are advised to stay off
the Jersey Turnpike...

01:54:15.454 --> 01:54:20.485
A'right. That's it. We're done. I'm
pulling us into the next motel.

01:54:20.509 --> 01:54:24.635
- Keep going as long as you can go Tony.
- I can't keep my eyes open.

01:54:24.806 --> 01:54:27.326
I'm getting hypnotized here.

01:54:27.681 --> 01:54:30.443
I think my brain's
gonna explode.

01:54:33.724 --> 01:54:36.236
Hey... we gave it a shot Doc.

01:54:36.380 --> 01:54:38.478
What you gonna do?

01:54:46.848 --> 01:54:50.899
Alright, the table is set, ladies and
gentlemen. Don't run in the house.

01:55:46.304 --> 01:55:49.449
Tony. Tony, wake up.

01:55:52.390 --> 01:55:56.629
- You alright?
- You're home, get inside.

01:56:12.149 --> 01:56:13.622
Goodnight.

01:56:14.219 --> 01:56:18.075
Wait, wait, come up,
meet my family...?

01:56:20.659 --> 01:56:22.968
Merry Christmas Tony.

01:56:27.547 --> 01:56:29.255
Merry Christmas!

01:57:06.461 --> 01:57:09.380
Look who it is,
Shakespeare's home!

01:57:17.990 --> 01:57:19.386
I made it back!

01:57:22.412 --> 01:57:24.768
Tony, God bless you!

01:57:37.890 --> 01:57:40.645
- You hungry?
- I'm starving.

01:57:56.628 --> 01:58:00.087
- Welcome home, Dr. Shirley.
- Thank you, Amit.

01:58:00.111 --> 01:58:03.571
I turned down your bed, sir.
Shall I unpack your luggage now?

01:58:03.595 --> 01:58:06.990
No, no, please. Go
home to your family.

01:58:07.155 --> 01:58:09.058
Thank you sir.

01:58:14.111 --> 01:58:17.818
- Merry Christmas Sir.
- Merry Christmas!

01:59:16.987 --> 01:59:19.609
Come on. You never kissed me like that.

01:59:22.557 --> 01:59:23.992
A'right, relax.

01:59:27.245 --> 01:59:30.788
So Tony, you alright? You
seem a little quite.

01:59:31.144 --> 01:59:34.515
Yeah, nah, I'm just tired.

01:59:35.183 --> 01:59:37.797
Long trip.

01:59:40.213 --> 01:59:43.390
You take care of that thing?

01:59:48.168 --> 01:59:51.259
- Thanks.
- Yeah, you owe me 75 bucks.

01:59:51.283 --> 01:59:54.678
Seventy five? Charlie said sixty.

01:59:54.799 --> 01:59:57.295
I'm doing this for free?

01:59:59.197 --> 02:00:03.837
Hey, Tony, tell us about the trip.
You're gone 2 months.

02:00:03.861 --> 02:00:06.702
Yeah. So how was he, the tootsune?
He get on your nerves?

02:00:07.146 --> 02:00:09.565
Don't call him that.

02:00:12.529 --> 02:00:14.589
Alright.

02:00:17.473 --> 02:00:20.719
Tony, you should have seen the day
last week when little Frankie

02:00:20.743 --> 02:00:24.494
climbed upon the TV. I took a
picture of him. He was so cute.

02:00:24.518 --> 02:00:26.103
He was so funny up there.

02:00:26.127 --> 02:00:30.140
What are you nuts, Dee? With all the tubes
back there, he could've got electrocuted!

02:00:51.686 --> 02:00:55.557
- Charlie?
- Hey Lip. Johnny invited me.

02:00:56.211 --> 02:01:00.021
- Well, come on in.
- You remember Marie?

02:01:00.051 --> 02:01:01.030
Hey Marie!

02:01:01.054 --> 02:01:04.189
Charlie, you actually came?
I was kidding?

02:01:04.849 --> 02:01:07.049
With the wife too?

02:01:07.099 --> 02:01:11.800
- Merry Christmas.
- Merry Christmas, hello! What a surprise!

02:01:11.824 --> 02:01:14.633
Everybody. Charlie from the pawn shop!

02:01:24.305 --> 02:01:26.240
Doc!

02:01:29.189 --> 02:01:30.991
Welcome!

02:01:34.196 --> 02:01:37.283
- Hey, everybody...
- Stop it, stop it.

02:01:37.307 --> 02:01:40.154
This is Dr Donald Shirley.

02:01:41.817 --> 02:01:43.829
Merry Christmas.

02:01:47.416 --> 02:01:51.663
Well, come on, make some room!
Get the man a plate!

02:01:59.543 --> 02:02:02.297
- Hello!
- You must be Dolores.

02:02:02.431 --> 02:02:05.951
- Welcome!
- Buon Natale.

02:02:07.055 --> 02:02:10.232
Thank you for sharing
your husband with me.

02:02:16.193 --> 02:02:19.917
Thank you for helping him
with the letters.

02:02:21.600 --> 02:02:25.613
Subtitled by CLARITY.
